{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TWhH61g8zw7uLWFnJ4MC5k","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Paper Type\n7\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n10\t\n11\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: 31–38% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001); within-subject range 31-45%, avg 38.1% (plan_014). This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n12\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement)\n13\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n14\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n17\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n18\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n19\t\n20\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n21\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n22\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n23\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n24\t\n25\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n26\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n27\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n28\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587.\n29\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n30\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33)\n31\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n32\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n33\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n34\t\n35\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n36\t\n37\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n38\t\n39\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n40\t\n41\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n42\t\n43\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n44\t\n45\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n46\t\n47\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n48\t\n49\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n50\t\n51\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n52\t\n53\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n54\t\n55\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n56\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n57\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n58\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n59\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n60\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n61\t- §6 Conclusion\n62\t\n63\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n64\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n65\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n66\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n67\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n68\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n69\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n70\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n71\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n72\t\n73\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n74\t\n75\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n76\t\n77\t## Venue Fit\n78\t\n79\t- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n80\t\n81\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n82\t\n83\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n84\t\n85\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n86\t\n87\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n88\t\n89\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n90\t\n91\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n92\t\n93\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n94\t\n95\t1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n96\t\n97\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n98\t\n99\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n100\t\n101\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n102\t\n103\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n104\t\n105\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n106\t\n107\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n108\t\n109\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n110\t\n111\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — Apply SIBTEST or logistic regression DIF to 5-10 representative subjects as robustness check. Show MH results are not missing substantial non-uniform DIF.\n112\t\n113\t10. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n114\t\n115\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n116\t\n117\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n118\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n119\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n120\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e8b678-023b-4cb0-b73e-f2db74cf2915","uuid":"eafc64df-c4ad-487a-91d1-207e9f0fc088","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:05:24.157Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T042647/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: 31–38% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001); within-subject range 31-45%, avg 38.1% (plan_014). This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — Apply SIBTEST or logistic regression DIF to 5-10 representative subjects as robustness check. Show MH results are not missing substantial non-uniform DIF.\n\n10. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RgKPHY5HCxDBJ98guMWbm4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MH-DIF on METABENCH MMLU (5,219 models × 12,508 items). Temporal, ability, within-family cohorts. Proxy validation against Li et al. labels. Domain-specificity analysis. SIBTEST robustness check added as worst-case critical experiment.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n7\t      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n8\t      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n9\t      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n10\t      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n11\t      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n12\t      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n13\t      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n14\t      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n15\t      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n16\t      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014,\n17\t      \"sibtest_nonuniform_additional_pct\": 22.4,\n18\t      \"mh_sibtest_flag_jaccard\": 0.48,\n19\t      \"sibtest_total_flagged_pct\": 44.7,\n20\t      \"sibtest_only_flags_pct\": 13.4,\n21\t      \"mh_only_flags_pct\": 8.9,\n22\t      \"sibtest_crossing_dif_items\": 1674\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      {\n26\t        \"name\": \"MH vs SIBTEST Flag Comparison (Temporal Cohort)\",\n27\t        \"columns\": [\n28\t          \"Method\",\n29\t          \"C_items\",\n30\t          \"C_pct\",\n31\t          \"Unique_flags\",\n32\t          \"Unique_pct\"\n33\t        ],\n34\t        \"rows\": [\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"MH (|Δ_MH|≥1.5)\",\n37\t            3918,\n38\t            31.3,\n39\t            1112,\n40\t            8.9\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"SIBTEST (β̂≥0.088)\",\n44\t            5592,\n45\t            44.7,\n46\t            1674,\n47\t            13.4\n48\t          ],\n49\t          [\n50\t            \"Intersection\",\n51\t            2806,\n52\t            22.4,\n53\t            \"—\",\n54\t            \"—\"\n55\t          ],\n56\t          [\n57\t            \"Union\",\n58\t            6584,\n59\t            52.7,\n60\t            \"—\",\n61\t            \"—\"\n62\t          ]\n63\t        ]\n64\t      },\n65\t      {\n66\t        \"name\": \"SIBTEST Non-uniform DIF by Subject Cluster\",\n67\t        \"columns\": [\n68\t          \"Subject_Cluster\",\n69\t          \"N_items\",\n70\t          \"Crossing_DIF_pct\",\n71\t          \"MH_missed_pct\"\n72\t        ],\n73\t        \"rows\": [\n74\t          [\n75\t            \"STEM_quantitative\",\n76\t            2841,\n77\t            28.3,\n78\t            18.7\n79\t          ],\n80\t          [\n81\t            \"STEM_conceptual\",\n82\t            1953,\n83\t            19.1,\n84\t            11.2\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"Humanities\",\n88\t            3287,\n89\t            24.6,\n90\t            14.8\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            \"Social_sciences\",\n94\t            2614,\n95\t            21.0,\n96\t            12.1\n97\t          ],\n98\t          [\n99\t            \"Professional\",\n100\t            1813,\n101\t            17.4,\n102\t            9.6\n103\t          ]\n104\t        ]\n105\t      }\n106\t    ],\n107\t    \"figures\": [],\n108\t    \"analysis\": \"SIBTEST结果对paper是结构性打击。31%不再是一个可靠的点估计——它是MH特异性的产物。 真实instability范围是18-45%（取决于方法和阈值），这使得任何基于31%的下游推断都变得 模糊。对于worst tier reframe：(1)将MH和SIBTEST结果并列报告，承认\\\"instability范围 ≥18-31%依赖于DIF类型和阈值\\\"而非捍卫单一数字；(2)crossing DIF的发现本身是有价值的 empirical contribution——\\\"MMLU items不仅在难度上漂移，还在区分功能上发生方向性变化\\\"； (3)这motivates更复杂的DIF方法（logistic regression DIF, MIMIC）作为future work。 但reviewer会说\\\"如果你自己的robustness check否定了headline number，为什么我们应该 相信这篇paper的任何具体数字？\\\"\\n\\n\\nMH结果本身不变（已有实际数据），但SIBTEST揭示了致命弱点：22.4%的items存在MH完全 遗漏的非均匀DIF（non-uniform/crossing DIF），即不同能力水平的模型在这些items上 表现出相反方向的DIF效应。MH只检测均匀位移，当DIF效应在能力谱上方向翻转时，正负 抵消导致Δ_MH≈0，这些items被MH判为clean。Jaccard=0.48说明两种方法标记的items重叠 不到一半——31%这个数字高度依赖于方法选择。1,674个crossing DIF items意味着MMLU中 存在大量\\\"对弱模型变难但对强模型变易\\\"（或反过来）的items，这种模式与contamination 的差异化机制高度一致（强模型更可能通过训练数据暴露获益），但MH的均匀性假设恰好 将其mask掉。这直接动摇了\\\"31%作为精确估计\\\"的可信度——真实instability可能在18%到 45%之间，取决于使用哪种DIF方法和哪个阈值。within-family分析中Llama-2 vs Llama-3 的61.3% C%进一步证实大量DIF反映的是capability gain而非contamination。\\n\"\n109\t  },\n110\t  {\n111\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n112\t    \"description\": \"验证DIF对RL训练的鲁棒性。SFT基线、alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477)、 reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO, 10-15 models)。群体级DIF稳定性+个体级传统检测器对比。\\n\",\n113\t    \"results\": {\n114\t      \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13,\n115\t      \"n_sft_baseline\": 312,\n116\t      \"n_alignment_rl\": 477,\n117\t      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_alignrl\": 0.71,\n118\t      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.58,\n119\t      \"dif_flag_jaccard_alignrl_vs_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.62,\n120\t      \"auroc_dif_sft\": 0.82,\n121\t      \"auroc_dif_alignrl\": 0.79,\n122\t      \"auroc_dif_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.64,\n123\t      \"auroc_constat_sft\": 0.74,\n124\t      \"auroc_constat_alignrl\": 0.68,\n125\t      \"auroc_constat_reasonrl\": 0.52,\n126\t      \"auroc_mink_sft\": 0.71,\n127\t      \"auroc_mink_alignrl\": 0.63,\n128\t      \"auroc_mink_reasonrl\": 0.41,\n129\t      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_sft_p\": 0.12,\n130\t      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_reasonrl_p\": 0.08,\n131\t      \"tost_equivalence_dif_sft_alignrl_p\": 0.03,\n132\t      \"tost_equivalence_dif_sft_reasonrl_p\": 0.31,\n133\t      \"detection_boundary_exploitation_rate\": 0.65,\n134\t      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif_reasonrl\": [\n135\t        0.41,\n136\t        0.84\n137\t      ],\n138\t      \"power_at_p04\": 0.18,\n139\t      \"power_at_p07\": 0.51,\n140\t      \"power_at_p10\": 0.64\n141\t    },\n142\t    \"tables\": [\n143\t      {\n144\t        \"name\": \"Detection Performance by Cohort Composition\",\n145\t        \"columns\": [\n146\t          \"Detector\",\n147\t          \"SFT_AUROC\",\n148\t          \"AlignRL_AUROC\",\n149\t          \"ReasonRL_AUROC\",\n150\t          \"Δ_SFT→ReasonRL\"\n151\t        ],\n152\t        \"rows\": [\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"DIF (MH)\",\n155\t            0.82,\n156\t            0.79,\n157\t            0.64,\n158\t            -0.18\n159\t          ],\n160\t          [\n161\t            \"ConStat\",\n162\t            0.74,\n163\t            0.68,\n164\t            0.52,\n165\t            -0.22\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"Min-K%\",\n169\t            0.71,\n170\t            0.63,\n171\t            0.41,\n172\t            -0.3\n173\t          ]\n174\t        ]\n175\t      },\n176\t      {\n177\t        \"name\": \"DIF Flag Stability Across Cohort Compositions\",\n178\t        \"columns\": [\n179\t          \"Comparison\",\n180\t          \"Jaccard\",\n181\t          \"New_flags\",\n182\t          \"Lost_flags\"\n183\t        ],\n184\t        \"rows\": [\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"SFT vs AlignRL\",\n187\t            0.71,\n188\t            412,\n189\t            287\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            \"SFT vs SFT+ReasonRL\",\n193\t            0.58,\n194\t            893,\n195\t            614\n196\t          ],\n197\t          [\n198\t            \"AlignRL vs AlignRL+ReasonRL\",\n199\t            0.62,\n200\t            731,\n201\t            508\n202\t          ]\n203\t        ]\n204\t      },\n205\t      {\n206\t        \"name\": \"TOST Equivalence Tests (Δ AUROC ≤ 0.10)\",\n207\t        \"columns\": [\n208\t          \"Comparison\",\n209\t          \"Δ_AUROC\",\n210\t          \"TOST_p\",\n211\t          \"Equivalent\"\n212\t        ],\n213\t        \"rows\": [\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"DIF: SFT vs AlignRL\",\n216\t            0.03,\n217\t            0.03,\n218\t            \"Yes\"\n219\t          ],\n220\t          [\n221\t            \"DIF: SFT vs ReasonRL\",\n222\t            0.18,\n223\t            0.31,\n224\t            \"No\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"ConStat: SFT vs ReasonRL\",\n228\t            0.22,\n229\t            0.44,\n230\t            \"No\"\n231\t          ]\n232\t        ]\n233\t      }\n234\t    ],\n235\t    \"figures\": [],\n236\t    \"analysis\": \"实验的根本问题是sample size。N=13 reasoning-RL模型不足以支撑任何统计推断—— 这不是\\\"underpowered\\\"可以轻描淡写的，而是使结论完全不可信。worst tier下reviewer 会直接说\\\"你声称DIF对RL robust但你只有13个RL模型，CI覆盖从random到excellent， 这不是evidence而是noise\\\"。对于reframe：将RL robustness完全降级到limitations/ future work，不在main claims中出现。承认\\\"RL robustness是open question，现有 METABENCH中reasoning-RL模型不足以验证\\\"。这反而增强了paper的诚实度。\\n\\n\\nN=13 reasoning-RL模型是致命瓶颈。当13个GRPO/PPO模型混入focal cohort时，cohort 总N仍≥80（满足DIF统计要求），但这些模型的contamination-masking效应使得DIF flag 集合发生实质性漂移（Jaccard从0.71降至0.58）。关键问题：AUROC在reasoning-RL条件下 降至0.64，bootstrap CI极宽[0.41, 0.84]——无法排除DIF在RL场景下接近random的可能。 TOST等价检验失败（p=0.31>>0.05），无法声称DIF对reasoning-RL是等价的。传统检测器 确实退化更多（ConStat 0.74→0.52, Min-K% 0.71→0.41），但DIF的退化也不小 （0.82→0.64），且DeLong检验p=0.08——差异不显著。这意味着\\\"DIF对RL鲁棒\\\"的声明 在统计上站不住脚。power analysis显示detection boundary在p≈0.65——只有>65% exploitation rate的contamination才能被检测到，这在实际中覆盖面有限。 整体结论：DIF比传统方法更robust是趋势性的，但N=13使得任何定量声明都不可信。\\n\"\n237\t  },\n238\t  {\n239\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n240\t    \"description\": \"ConStat-style perturbation testing独立评估。200+ MMLU items语义等价改写， FDR-controlled detection，与DIF对比。\\n\",\n241\t    \"results\": {\n242\t      \"n_items_reformulated\": 237,\n243\t      \"n_models_tested\": 48,\n244\t      \"constat_detection_rate_non_rl\": 0.34,\n245\t      \"constat_detection_rate_rl\": 0.11,\n246\t      \"constat_fdr_controlled_rate\": 0.28,\n247\t      \"constat_fpr\": 0.067,\n248\t      \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.78,\n249\t      \"constat_auroc_rl\": 0.54,\n250\t      \"dif_auroc_same_items\": 0.73,\n251\t      \"dif_constat_overlap_flagged\": 0.31,\n252\t      \"paraphrase_quality_human_eval\": 0.82,\n253\t      \"paraphrase_semantic_sim\": 0.91,\n254\t      \"effect_size_non_rl_mean_d\": 0.87,\n255\t      \"effect_size_rl_mean_d\": 0.34\n256\t    },\n257\t    \"tables\": [\n258\t      {\n259\t        \"name\": \"ConStat vs DIF Detection Comparison\",\n260\t        \"columns\": [\n261\t          \"Metric\",\n262\t          \"ConStat\",\n263\t          \"DIF (MH)\",\n264\t          \"Advantage\"\n265\t        ],\n266\t        \"rows\": [\n267\t          [\n268\t            \"AUROC (non-RL)\",\n269\t            0.78,\n270\t            0.73,\n271\t            \"ConStat +0.05\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"AUROC (RL)\",\n275\t            0.54,\n276\t            0.64,\n277\t            \"DIF +0.10\"\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"FPR\",\n281\t            0.067,\n282\t            0.314,\n283\t            \"ConStat ×4.7 better\"\n284\t          ],\n285\t          [\n286\t            \"Per-model granularity\",\n287\t            \"Yes\",\n288\t            \"No\",\n289\t            \"ConStat\"\n290\t          ],\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"Flag overlap (Jaccard)\",\n293\t            \"—\",\n294\t            \"—\",\n295\t            0.31\n296\t          ]\n297\t        ]\n298\t      }\n299\t    ],\n300\t    \"figures\": [],\n301\t    \"analysis\": \"ConStat结果对DIF-as-contamination-detector叙事构成直接竞争。在non-RL场景下ConStat 更精确（低FPR）且粒度更细（per-model），这使得DIF在contamination detection赛道上 处于劣势。但这实际上支持了worst tier的reframe方向：DIF不应该定位为contamination detector，而是benchmark stability characterization工具——两者检测的是不同信号 （ConStat检测specific model anomaly，DIF检测cross-cohort item property shift）。 Reframe后ConStat变成complementary baseline而非competing method。\\n\\n\\nConStat在per-model detection上展现出DIF不具备的粒度优势：它可以指出具体哪个模型 在哪些items上表现异常（FPR=0.067远低于DIF的temporal baseline 0.31）。在non-RL 模型上AUROC=0.78略高于DIF的0.73（同一items子集），这使得reviewer有理由质疑 \\\"为什么不直接用ConStat而要用这个baseline FPR=31%的老方法？\\\"。RL条件下ConStat 确实退化严重（0.78→0.54），但DIF在worst tier下也退化（plan_002: 0.82→0.64）， 差异不如expected那么戏剧性。关键攻击点：ConStat的FPR（0.067）比DIF temporal的 FPR（0.31）低一个数量级——reviewer会问\\\"你的方法31%的items被flagged作为baseline， 另一个方法只有6.7% false positive，哪个更可信？\\\"。overlap仅0.31说明两种方法 检测的是根本不同的信号——这在worst tier下被解读为\\\"DIF检测的不是contamination 而是别的什么东西\\\"。\\n\"\n302\t  },\n303\t  {\n304\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n305\t    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance独立评估。10-15个open-weight模型，50 responses/item， generation variance scores，bimodal distribution检测。\\n\",\n306\t    \"results\": {\n307\t      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n308\t      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n309\t      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n310\t      \"dvd_auroc_verbatim\": 0.69,\n311\t      \"dvd_auroc_variant\": 0.58,\n312\t      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.089,\n313\t      \"dvd_bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.23,\n314\t      \"dvd_effect_size_verbatim_d\": 0.74,\n315\t      \"dvd_effect_size_variant_d\": 0.41,\n316\t      \"dvd_dif_overlap_flagged\": 0.19,\n317\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 63,\n318\t      \"temperature_sensitivity_t07_auroc\": 0.69,\n319\t      \"temperature_sensitivity_t10_auroc\": 0.62\n320\t    },\n321\t    \"tables\": [\n322\t      {\n323\t        \"name\": \"DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n324\t        \"columns\": [\n325\t          \"Contamination_Type\",\n326\t          \"N_items\",\n327\t          \"AUROC\",\n328\t          \"Bimodal_pct\",\n329\t          \"Effect_d\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"rows\": [\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"Verbatim\",\n334\t            127,\n335\t            0.69,\n336\t            31.5,\n337\t            0.74\n338\t          ],\n339\t          [\n340\t            \"Variant\",\n341\t            89,\n342\t            0.58,\n343\t            12.4,\n344\t            0.41\n345\t          ],\n346\t          [\n347\t            \"Clean\",\n348\t            284,\n349\t            \"—\",\n350\t            4.2,\n351\t            \"—\"\n352\t          ]\n353\t        ]\n354\t      },\n355\t      {\n356\t        \"name\": \"DVD vs DIF Signal Comparison\",\n357\t        \"columns\": [\n358\t          \"Metric\",\n359\t          \"DVD\",\n360\t          \"DIF\",\n361\t          \"Overlap_Jaccard\"\n362\t        ],\n363\t        \"rows\": [\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"Items flagged\",\n366\t            94,\n367\t            157,\n368\t            0.19\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"FPR\",\n372\t            0.089,\n373\t            0.314,\n374\t            \"—\"\n375\t          ],\n376\t          [\n377\t            \"Detection granularity\",\n378\t            \"per-model\",\n379\t            \"per-cohort\",\n380\t            \"—\"\n381\t          ]\n382\t        ]\n383\t      }\n384\t    ],\n385\t    \"figures\": [],\n386\t    \"analysis\": \"DVD结果确认了generation variance作为contamination signal的局限性——在variant contamination（更现实的场景）上几乎失效。但这不直接伤害DIF叙事，因为DVD和DIF 检测的是完全不同的信号（Jaccard=0.19）。在worst tier reframe中，DVD结果变成 \\\"motivating example for why single-signal detection is insufficient\\\"——但由于 ensemble（plan_003c）也不work well，这个motivating example没有resolution。\\n\\n\\nDVD的per-model generation variance检测在verbatim contamination上表现中等 （AUROC=0.69），variant contamination上较弱（0.58）。与DIF的flag overlap极低 （0.19），再次表明不同方法检测不同类型的信号。DVD的核心假设——contaminated items 产生bimodal response分布——在实际LLM上只有23%的known-contaminated items表现出 明显bimodality，这是因为现代LLM在temperature=0.7时already highly consistent， contamination造成的额外consistency增量很小。GPU cost=63hrs使其成为expensive的 detection method（DIF是zero GPU cost）。在worst tier下，DVD结果是\\\"another incomplete signal\\\"——既不强到取代DIF，也不弱到让DIF显得indispensable，陷入 \\\"所有方法都partially work\\\"的尴尬叙事。\\n\"\n387\t  },\n388\t  {\n389\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n390\t    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD三信号融合。阈值校准，majority voting，weighted fusion， 5-fold cross-validation。\\n\",\n391\t    \"results\": {\n392\t      \"ensemble_2of3_auroc\": 0.72,\n393\t      \"ensemble_weighted_auroc\": 0.76,\n394\t      \"ensemble_fpr\": 0.112,\n395\t      \"best_single_signal_auroc\": 0.78,\n396\t      \"ensemble_vs_best_single_delong_p\": 0.38,\n397\t      \"ensemble_coverage_high_delta\": 0.81,\n398\t      \"ensemble_coverage_low_delta\": 0.43,\n399\t      \"ensemble_coverage_rl\": 0.48,\n400\t      \"cv_fold_variance_auroc\": 0.034,\n401\t      \"uniform_weight_auroc\": 0.71,\n402\t      \"optimized_weight_dif\": 0.28,\n403\t      \"optimized_weight_constat\": 0.47,\n404\t      \"optimized_weight_dvd\": 0.25,\n405\t      \"fpr_above_010_configs\": 3,\n406\t      \"total_configs_tested\": 8\n407\t    },\n408\t    \"tables\": [\n409\t      {\n410\t        \"name\": \"Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance\",\n411\t        \"columns\": [\n412\t          \"Method\",\n413\t          \"AUROC\",\n414\t          \"FPR\",\n415\t          \"Coverage_δ≥1.4\",\n416\t          \"Coverage_δ<1.0\"\n417\t        ],\n418\t        \"rows\": [\n419\t          [\n420\t            \"DIF alone\",\n421\t            0.73,\n422\t            0.314,\n423\t            0.79,\n424\t            0.22\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"ConStat alone\",\n428\t            0.78,\n429\t            0.067,\n430\t            0.61,\n431\t            0.48\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"DVD alone\",\n435\t            0.69,\n436\t            0.089,\n437\t            0.54,\n438\t            0.37\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"Ensemble (2-of-3)\",\n442\t            0.72,\n443\t            0.048,\n444\t            0.52,\n445\t            0.31\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"Ensemble (weighted)\",\n449\t            0.76,\n450\t            0.112,\n451\t            0.81,\n452\t            0.43\n453\t          ]\n454\t        ]\n455\t      },\n456\t      {\n457\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Validation Stability\",\n458\t        \"columns\": [\n459\t          \"Fold\",\n460\t          \"AUROC\",\n461\t          \"w_DIF\",\n462\t          \"w_ConStat\",\n463\t          \"w_DVD\"\n464\t        ],\n465\t        \"rows\": [\n466\t          [\n467\t            1,\n468\t            0.79,\n469\t            0.31,\n470\t            0.44,\n471\t            0.25\n472\t          ],\n473\t          [\n474\t            2,\n475\t            0.74,\n476\t            0.22,\n477\t            0.52,\n478\t            0.26\n479\t          ],\n480\t          [\n481\t            3,\n482\t            0.78,\n483\t            0.35,\n484\t            0.41,\n485\t            0.24\n486\t          ],\n487\t          [\n488\t            4,\n489\t            0.72,\n490\t            0.19,\n491\t            0.53,\n492\t            0.28\n493\t          ],\n494\t          [\n495\t            5,\n496\t            0.77,\n497\t            0.33,\n498\t            0.45,\n499\t            0.22\n500\t          ]\n501\t        ]\n502\t      }\n503\t    ],\n504\t    \"figures\": [],\n505\t    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble failure在worst tier叙事中有两种解读：(1)消极——DIF不是一个有价值的 ensemble component，整个multi-signal方向是dead end；(2)积极（reframe后）—— 这说明contamination detection fundamentally不能通过简单signal combination解决， 需要新方法论。但后者是一个non-result dressed up as insight，reviewer不会buy。 对于reframe：将ensemble完全移到appendix/future work，main paper不再声称 detection improvement，而是聚焦于characterization和framework贡献。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble的核心承诺是\\\"coverage handoff\\\"——DIF覆盖high-delta，ConStat覆盖non-RL medium-delta，DVD覆盖variant。但实际融合结果令人失望：weighted AUROC=0.76低于 ConStat单独的0.78，DeLong p=0.38表明ensemble没有统计显著地超越最佳单信号。 这是因为三个信号的correlation structure不利于融合：DIF和ConStat在某些items上 产生contradictory signals（DIF flag但ConStat clean，或反过来），majority voting 在这种情况下倾向于conservative（2-of-3需要agreement），而weighted fusion的 DIF权重被压低到0.28（反映其高baseline FPR降低了fusion中的信息价值）。 FPR=0.112超过了0.10目标阈值（3/8 configurations）。CV fold variance=0.034 说明权重unstable。在worst tier下，ensemble failure是\\\"the punchline that never lands\\\"——paper承诺了complementary detection但deliver的是noise averaging。 Reviewer会说\\\"如果ensemble不比单方法好，为什么这是一个contribution？\\\"\\n\"\n506\t  },\n507\t  {\n508\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n509\t    \"description\": \"GSM8K DIF复制 + GSM1K ground truth验证。Temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models。Semi-synthetic validation。GSM1K correlation with difficulty control。\\n\",\n510\t    \"results\": {\n511\t      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_dif\": {\n512\t        \"n_items\": 1319,\n513\t        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n514\t        \"n_foc\": 804,\n515\t        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n516\t        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n517\t        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3\n518\t      },\n519\t      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n520\t        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n521\t        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517\n522\t      },\n523\t      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n524\t        \"n_models\": 33,\n525\t        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n526\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n527\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n528\t        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n529\t        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n530\t        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n531\t        \"partial_r_controlling_difficulty\": -0.08,\n532\t        \"partial_p_difficulty\": 0.67,\n533\t        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy_and_difficulty\": 0.03,\n534\t        \"partial_p_acc_diff\": 0.87,\n535\t        \"difficulty_control_ci_lower\": -0.31,\n536\t        \"difficulty_control_ci_upper\": 0.15,\n537\t        \"permutation_p_difficulty_controlled\": 0.64,\n538\t        \"dif_item_mean_difficulty\": 0.38,\n539\t        \"non_dif_item_mean_difficulty\": 0.61,\n540\t        \"difficulty_dif_correlation\": -0.52\n541\t      }\n542\t    },\n543\t    \"tables\": [\n544\t      {\n545\t        \"name\": \"GSM1K Correlation Under Progressive Controls\",\n546\t        \"columns\": [\n547\t          \"Model\",\n548\t          \"r\",\n549\t          \"p\",\n550\t          \"95% CI\",\n551\t          \"Interpretation\"\n552\t        ],\n553\t        \"rows\": [\n554\t          [\n555\t            \"Bivariate\",\n556\t            -0.478,\n557\t            0.005,\n558\t            \"[-0.71, -0.16]\",\n559\t            \"Significant\"\n560\t          ],\n561\t          [\n562\t            \"Partial (acc)\",\n563\t            -0.385,\n564\t            0.027,\n565\t            \"[-0.64, -0.06]\",\n566\t            \"Significant\"\n567\t          ],\n568\t          [\n569\t            \"Partial (difficulty)\",\n570\t            -0.08,\n571\t            0.67,\n572\t            \"[-0.31, 0.15]\",\n573\t            \"Non-significant\"\n574\t          ],\n575\t          [\n576\t            \"Partial (acc+difficulty)\",\n577\t            0.03,\n578\t            0.87,\n579\t            \"[-0.22, 0.28]\",\n580\t            \"Null\"\n581\t          ]\n582\t        ]\n583\t      },\n584\t      {\n585\t        \"name\": \"DIF-C vs Non-DIF Item Difficulty\",\n586\t        \"columns\": [\n587\t          \"Item_Group\",\n588\t          \"N\",\n589\t          \"Mean_p_value\",\n590\t          \"SD\",\n591\t          \"Mean_discrimination\"\n592\t        ],\n593\t        \"rows\": [\n594\t          [\n595\t            \"DIF-C\",\n596\t            249,\n597\t            0.38,\n598\t            0.21,\n599\t            0.42\n600\t          ],\n601\t          [\n602\t            \"Non-DIF\",\n603\t            1070,\n604\t            0.61,\n605\t            0.24,\n606\t            0.39\n607\t          ],\n608\t          [\n609\t            \"t-test p\",\n610\t            \"—\",\n611\t            \"<0.001\",\n612\t            \"—\",\n613\t            0.34\n614\t          ]\n615\t        ]\n616\t      }\n617\t    ],\n618\t    \"figures\": [],\n619\t    \"analysis\": \"GSM1K correlation collapse是worst tier的defining feature之一。Sub-finding 4 从paper的main body中完全删除。ρ≈0.997 redundancy和circularity ablation（z=-9.5） 不受影响（它们不依赖GSM1K）。Reframe后Claim 4缩减为三个sub-finding：(1)redundancy， (2)DIF≠high-discrimination（circularity ablation），(3)diagnostic lens（model-specific patterns）。GSM8K的Step 1和Step 2仍然有用——framework portability demonstration survives，只是downstream validation不work了。\\n\\n\\nStep 1和Step 2的结果不变（已有实际数据），关键崩塌发生在Step 3的difficulty control。 原始r=-0.478看似strong，但DIF-C items系统性地更难（mean p-value=0.38 vs 0.61）， difficulty与DIF-C flag的correlation=-0.52。当控制item difficulty后，partial r从-0.385骤降至-0.08（p=0.67），CI=[-0.31, 0.15]稳固包含零。同时控制accuracy 和difficulty后，r→0.03（essentially zero）。这意味着原始correlation完全由 confound驱动：DIF flags harder items → harder items have larger contamination gaps (floor effect) → spurious negative correlation。这不是DIF-C items \\\"resist contamination\\\" 而是 \\\"DIF-C items are harder, and harder items have smaller accuracy differences between GSM8K and GSM1K regardless of contamination\\\"。 N=33的小样本加剧了问题——控制一个confound就吃掉所有degrees of freedom。 Sub-finding 4（DIF items resist contamination-based gains）在difficulty control下彻底死亡。\\n\"\n620\t  },\n621\t  {\n622\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n623\t    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating pilot on MMLU。General factor + 57 subject-specific factors。Anchor item selection。Fixed-parameter calibration。Score equivalence validation (target ρ≥0.95)。\\n\",\n624\t    \"results\": {\n625\t      \"model_convergence\": \"partial\",\n626\t      \"n_iterations_to_convergence\": 8500,\n627\t      \"convergence_criterion_met\": false,\n628\t      \"rmsea\": 0.047,\n629\t      \"cfi\": 0.72,\n630\t      \"tli\": 0.69,\n631\t      \"srmr\": 0.081,\n632\t      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.31,\n633\t      \"specific_factor_avg_variance\": 0.18,\n634\t      \"residual_variance\": 0.51,\n635\t      \"n_anchor_items_identified\": 847,\n636\t      \"anchor_item_stability_criterion\": 0.8,\n637\t      \"n_items_meeting_stability\": 412,\n638\t      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_10pct\": 0.91,\n639\t      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_20pct\": 0.86,\n640\t      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_31pct\": 0.79,\n641\t      \"score_equivalence_bias_mean\": 0.34,\n642\t      \"score_equivalence_bias_max\": 2.17\n643\t    },\n644\t    \"tables\": [\n645\t      {\n646\t        \"name\": \"Bifactor Model Fit Indices\",\n647\t        \"columns\": [\n648\t          \"Index\",\n649\t          \"Value\",\n650\t          \"Acceptable\",\n651\t          \"Good\",\n652\t          \"Status\"\n653\t        ],\n654\t        \"rows\": [\n655\t          [\n656\t            \"RMSEA\",\n657\t            0.047,\n658\t            \"<0.08\",\n659\t            \"<0.05\",\n660\t            \"Borderline\"\n661\t          ],\n662\t          [\n663\t            \"CFI\",\n664\t            0.72,\n665\t            \">0.90\",\n666\t            \">0.95\",\n667\t            \"FAIL\"\n668\t          ],\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"TLI\",\n671\t            0.69,\n672\t            \">0.90\",\n673\t            \">0.95\",\n674\t            \"FAIL\"\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            \"SRMR\",\n678\t            0.081,\n679\t            \"<0.08\",\n680\t            \"<0.05\",\n681\t            \"FAIL\"\n682\t          ]\n683\t        ]\n684\t      },\n685\t      {\n686\t        \"name\": \"Score Equivalence After Item Replacement\",\n687\t        \"columns\": [\n688\t          \"Replacement_pct\",\n689\t          \"Spearman_ρ\",\n690\t          \"Mean_bias\",\n691\t          \"Max_bias\",\n692\t          \"Target_met\"\n693\t        ],\n694\t        \"rows\": [\n695\t          [\n696\t            \"5%\",\n697\t            0.94,\n698\t            0.12,\n699\t            0.87,\n700\t            \"No (ρ<0.95)\"\n701\t          ],\n702\t          [\n703\t            \"10%\",\n704\t            0.91,\n705\t            0.34,\n706\t            1.41,\n707\t            \"No\"\n708\t          ],\n709\t          [\n710\t            \"20%\",\n711\t            0.86,\n712\t            0.67,\n713\t            1.89,\n714\t            \"No\"\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            \"31%\",\n718\t            0.79,\n719\t            1.12,\n720\t            2.17,\n721\t            \"No\"\n722\t          ]\n723\t        ]\n724\t      }\n725\t    ],\n726\t    \"figures\": [],\n727\t    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor pilot的失败confirmed paper_framing.md中已经预期的结论：\\\"IRT是fundamentally misspecified for MMLU\\\"。这在worst tier下被reviewer weaponize：\\\"如果你承认IRT misspecified，那MH conditioning on total score是唯一defensible approach—— 但then 31% reflects score-based rather than ability-based DIF，你没有evidence 这是'真正的'item functioning差异而不是score distribution artifact\\\"。 Equating pilot失败意味着Claim 3（regeneration）完全dead。对于reframe：将equating 从claims中完全移除，bifactor结果变成limitations section的evidence——\\\"future work 需要multidimensional IRT才能实现equating\\\"。\\n\\n\\nBifactor模型在5,219×12,508矩阵上面临计算和统计双重困难。模型未完全收敛（8,500 iterations仍未满足criterion），CFI=0.72和TLI=0.69远低于acceptable fit标准（>0.90）。 这并非意外——MMLU的57 subjects构成的multidimensional structure过于复杂，bifactor 是一个over-simplification（假设1个general factor + 57 orthogonal specific factors， 但实际上subjects之间存在大量cross-loading）。General factor仅解释31%方差，说明 MMLU的\\\"general intelligence\\\"维度很弱。残差方差51%意味着模型miss了一半的信号。\\nAnchor item selection结果更差：按stability criterion(across-cohort Δ_MH<0.5) 筛选出847个候选anchor items，但只有412个满足更严格的equating stability要求。 用这412个anchor做fixed-parameter calibration后，替换10%的items时ρ=0.91（<0.95 target），替换31%时ρ=0.79——远低于目标。Score equivalence bias高达2.17， 意味着某些模型的equated score偏移>2个标准误。\\n根本原因：IRT equating假设latent trait是well-measured的，但MMLU上1D IRT fundamentally misspecified（98% models |Lz|>2），bifactor虽然better但仍然 inadequate。Without good person parameter estimates, equating is garbage-in- garbage-out。\\n\"\n728\t  },\n729\t  {\n730\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n731\t    \"description\": \"LLM生成替换items + student simulation校准。Construct constraints, difficulty estimation, holdout validation。\\n\",\n732\t    \"results\": {\n733\t      \"n_items_generated\": 500,\n734\t      \"n_items_passing_face_validity\": 312,\n735\t      \"face_validity_pass_rate\": 0.624,\n736\t      \"difficulty_correlation_prompt_based\": 0.31,\n737\t      \"difficulty_correlation_student_sim\": 0.52,\n738\t      \"difficulty_correlation_target\": 0.75,\n739\t      \"subject_coverage_pct\": 89,\n740\t      \"cognitive_level_match_pct\": 67,\n741\t      \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.48,\n742\t      \"discrimination_match_r\": 0.29,\n743\t      \"construct_drift_detected_pct\": 18.4,\n744\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 178\n745\t    },\n746\t    \"tables\": [\n747\t      {\n748\t        \"name\": \"Item Generation Quality Metrics\",\n749\t        \"columns\": [\n750\t          \"Metric\",\n751\t          \"Value\",\n752\t          \"Target\",\n753\t          \"Status\"\n754\t        ],\n755\t        \"rows\": [\n756\t          [\n757\t            \"Face validity pass rate\",\n758\t            0.624,\n759\t            \">0.80\",\n760\t            \"FAIL\"\n761\t          ],\n762\t          [\n763\t            \"Difficulty ρ (prompt-based)\",\n764\t            0.31,\n765\t            \"0.45+\",\n766\t            \"FAIL\"\n767\t          ],\n768\t          [\n769\t            \"Difficulty ρ (student sim)\",\n770\t            0.52,\n771\t            \"0.75+\",\n772\t            \"FAIL\"\n773\t          ],\n774\t          [\n775\t            \"Discrimination match r\",\n776\t            0.29,\n777\t            \">0.60\",\n778\t            \"FAIL\"\n779\t          ],\n780\t          [\n781\t            \"Construct drift\",\n782\t            \"18.4%\",\n783\t            \"<5%\",\n784\t            \"FAIL\"\n785\t          ],\n786\t          [\n787\t            \"Holdout ranking ρ\",\n788\t            0.48,\n789\t            \"≥0.95\",\n790\t            \"FAIL\"\n791\t          ]\n792\t        ]\n793\t      }\n794\t    ],\n795\t    \"figures\": [],\n796\t    \"analysis\": \"Item generation失败在worst tier reframe中不造成额外伤害——regeneration（Claim 3 原版）已经在Dream #3中被pruned to appendix。但这个negative result本身有publication value作为\\\"cautionary tale about LLM-based item generation for high-stakes benchmarks\\\"——如果space permits可以在Discussion中brief mention。\\n\\n\\nItem generation面临两个层面的困难。First, face validity：只有62.4%的generated items通过human evaluation（incorrect distractors太obvious，或者stem在语义上 偏移了原item的construct）。Second, calibration：student simulation的difficulty estimation（ρ=0.52）远低于arXiv 2601.09953报告的0.75-0.82，这是因为MMLU items 的difficulty主要由knowledge specificity驱动（而非reasoning complexity），而LLM student simulation更擅长估计reasoning difficulty。Discrimination match更差 （r=0.29）——generated items的区分度系统性偏低，因为LLM倾向于生成\\\"textbook-style\\\" 的clean items而非real exam的nuanced items。\\n18.4%的construct drift意味着近五分之一的生成items实际上测量的是不同的construct—— 比如原item测试\\\"specific legal precedent knowledge\\\"但generated item测试 \\\"general legal reasoning\\\"。这在holdout panel上表现为ρ=0.48——生成的benchmark 与原始benchmark的model ranking correlation很弱。\\nCombined with plan_005的equating failure，整个regeneration pipeline（Claim 3原版） 在worst tier下是完全不可行的。\\n\"\n797\t  },\n798\t  {\n799\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n800\t    \"description\": \"Cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006)。4轮successive administrations模拟。Power improvement from evidence accumulation。\\n\",\n801\t    \"results\": {\n802\t      \"individual_admin_power_delta10\": 0.41,\n803\t      \"cumulative_2admin_power_delta10\": 0.52,\n804\t      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta10\": 0.58,\n805\t      \"cumulative_4admin_power_delta10\": 0.63,\n806\t      \"target_cumulative_3admin_power\": 0.7,\n807\t      \"target_met\": false,\n808\t      \"prior_calibration_error_mean\": 0.23,\n809\t      \"prior_calibration_error_max\": 0.67,\n810\t      \"fpr_inflation_cumulative_4admin\": 0.074,\n811\t      \"bayesian_mh_correlation_flags\": 0.81,\n812\t      \"bayes_factor_median\": 3.2,\n813\t      \"bayes_factor_gt10_pct\": 18.4,\n814\t      \"simulation_n_per_admin\": 200,\n815\t      \"n_items_simulated\": 1000,\n816\t      \"n_administrations\": 4\n817\t    },\n818\t    \"tables\": [\n819\t      {\n820\t        \"name\": \"Cumulative Power by Administration\",\n821\t        \"columns\": [\n822\t          \"N_admins\",\n823\t          \"Power_δ=0.8\",\n824\t          \"Power_δ=1.0\",\n825\t          \"Power_δ=1.4\",\n826\t          \"FPR\"\n827\t        ],\n828\t        \"rows\": [\n829\t          [\n830\t            1,\n831\t            0.22,\n832\t            0.41,\n833\t            0.68,\n834\t            0.042\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            2,\n838\t            0.31,\n839\t            0.52,\n840\t            0.76,\n841\t            0.051\n842\t          ],\n843\t          [\n844\t            3,\n845\t            0.37,\n846\t            0.58,\n847\t            0.81,\n848\t            0.063\n849\t          ],\n850\t          [\n851\t            4,\n852\t            0.42,\n853\t            0.63,\n854\t            0.84,\n855\t            0.074\n856\t          ]\n857\t        ]\n858\t      },\n859\t      {\n860\t        \"name\": \"Prior Calibration Analysis\",\n861\t        \"columns\": [\n862\t          \"Admin_pair\",\n863\t          \"Prior_mean_error\",\n864\t          \"Prior_var_error\",\n865\t          \"BF_median\"\n866\t        ],\n867\t        \"rows\": [\n868\t          [\n869\t            \"1→2\",\n870\t            0.14,\n871\t            0.08,\n872\t            4.1\n873\t          ],\n874\t          [\n875\t            \"2→3\",\n876\t            0.21,\n877\t            0.13,\n878\t            3.4\n879\t          ],\n880\t          [\n881\t            \"3→4\",\n882\t            0.34,\n883\t            0.19,\n884\t            2.7\n885\t          ]\n886\t        ]\n887\t      }\n888\t    ],\n889\t    \"figures\": [],\n890\t    \"analysis\": \"Bayesian cumulative DIF在worst tier下确认了paper_framing.md的decision to move it to appendix。Power improvement不足以justify complexity increase。 Prior miscalibration问题是fundamental——LLM benchmark \\\"administrations\\\" 不满足Bayesian updating的stationarity assumption。在reframe后，这变成 appendix material：\\\"simulation study showing theoretical potential with caveats about non-stationary populations\\\"。\\n\\n\\nCumulative Bayesian方法的power improvement低于理论预期：3-admin cumulative power=0.58（vs target 0.70），4-admin才达到0.63。差距来自prior miscalibration： Sinharay et al.的priors是为human testing设计的（student populations with stable demographics），LLM \\\"administrations\\\"的cohort composition变化更剧烈 （每轮新模型的ability distribution shift更大），导致informative priors反而 引入bias。Prior calibration error mean=0.23意味着prior对DIF effect size的 预期系统性偏离了actual，累积后bias不是减少而是compound。\\nBayes factors偏弱（median=3.2，只有18.4%的items BF>10），说明evidence accumulation受限于LLM cohort间的non-stationarity。FPR inflation到0.074 在4-admin后是manageable但concerning——累积更多administrations可能会worse。\\n与MH flags的correlation=0.81说明Bayesian方法在很大程度上agree with MH， 增量贡献有限——essentially adding computational complexity for modest gain。\\n\"\n891\t  },\n892\t  {\n893\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n894\t    \"description\": \"Benchmark validity under progressive item replacement。Ranking stability, score reliability, construct coverage at 5/10/20/50% replacement。 Theoretical bounds + empirical validation on METABENCH。\\n\",\n895\t    \"results\": {\n896\t      \"rho_5pct_replacement\": 0.993,\n897\t      \"rho_10pct_replacement\": 0.984,\n898\t      \"rho_20pct_replacement\": 0.961,\n899\t      \"rho_50pct_replacement\": 0.887,\n900\t      \"reliability_original_kr20\": 0.967,\n901\t      \"reliability_5pct\": 0.964,\n902\t      \"reliability_10pct\": 0.958,\n903\t      \"reliability_20pct\": 0.943,\n904\t      \"reliability_50pct\": 0.891,\n905\t      \"construct_coverage_original\": 1.0,\n906\t      \"construct_coverage_5pct\": 0.98,\n907\t      \"construct_coverage_10pct\": 0.95,\n908\t      \"construct_coverage_20pct\": 0.87,\n909\t      \"construct_coverage_50pct\": 0.71,\n910\t      \"theoretical_lower_bound_rho_at_31pct\": 0.92,\n911\t      \"empirical_rho_at_31pct\": 0.94,\n912\t      \"critical_replacement_threshold\": 0.23,\n913\t      \"validity_degradation_rate\": \"nonlinear\"\n914\t    },\n915\t    \"tables\": [\n916\t      {\n917\t        \"name\": \"Validity Metrics Under Progressive Replacement\",\n918\t        \"columns\": [\n919\t          \"Replace_pct\",\n920\t          \"Rank_ρ\",\n921\t          \"KR-20\",\n922\t          \"Coverage\",\n923\t          \"Max_rank_shift\"\n924\t        ],\n925\t        \"rows\": [\n926\t          [\n927\t            \"0% (original)\",\n928\t            1.0,\n929\t            0.967,\n930\t            1.0,\n931\t            0\n932\t          ],\n933\t          [\n934\t            \"5%\",\n935\t            0.993,\n936\t            0.964,\n937\t            0.98,\n938\t            23\n939\t          ],\n940\t          [\n941\t            \"10%\",\n942\t            0.984,\n943\t            0.958,\n944\t            0.95,\n945\t            47\n946\t          ],\n947\t          [\n948\t            \"20%\",\n949\t            0.961,\n950\t            0.943,\n951\t            0.87,\n952\t            112\n953\t          ],\n954\t          [\n955\t            \"31% (DIF rate)\",\n956\t            0.94,\n957\t            0.927,\n958\t            0.79,\n959\t            189\n960\t          ],\n961\t          [\n962\t            \"50%\",\n963\t            0.887,\n964\t            0.891,\n965\t            0.71,\n966\t            341\n967\t          ]\n968\t        ]\n969\t      },\n970\t      {\n971\t        \"name\": \"Theoretical vs Empirical Degradation\",\n972\t        \"columns\": [\n973\t          \"Replace_pct\",\n974\t          \"Theory_lower_ρ\",\n975\t          \"Empirical_ρ\",\n976\t          \"Gap\"\n977\t        ],\n978\t        \"rows\": [\n979\t          [\n980\t            \"10%\",\n981\t            0.978,\n982\t            0.984,\n983\t            \"+0.006\"\n984\t          ],\n985\t          [\n986\t            \"20%\",\n987\t            0.944,\n988\t            0.961,\n989\t            \"+0.017\"\n990\t          ],\n991\t          [\n992\t            \"31%\",\n993\t            0.92,\n994\t            0.94,\n995\t            \"+0.020\"\n996\t          ],\n997\t          [\n998\t            \"50%\",\n999\t            0.868,\n1000\t            0.887,\n1001\t            \"+0.019\"\n1002\t          ]\n1003\t        ]\n1004\t      }\n1005\t    ],\n1006\t    \"figures\": [],\n1007\t    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation在worst tier reframe中降级为supplementary analysis。 核心insight（replacement threshold < DIF rate）在appendix中作为\\\"the fundamental tension in DIF-based benchmark maintenance\\\"讨论，但不作为main claim。ρ≈0.997 的existing finding（plan_017, DIF removal without replacement）remains the stronger and simpler message for the main paper。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation分析本身产生reasonable results——rankings在20%替换时 仍robust（ρ=0.961），但construct coverage更fragile（0.87 at 20%）。关键 问题在worst tier context中：这个分析假设replacement items是well-calibrated的， 但plan_005（equating failure）和plan_006（generation failure）已经证明 实际的replacement items质量远低于预期。所以degradation curves是optimistic lower bound——实际degradation会worse。\\nCritical replacement threshold=23%意味着替换>23%的items时validity开始 non-linearly degrade。但我们的DIF flag rate是31%——超过了这个threshold。 Reviewer会指出：\\\"你说31%的items unstable，但你也说替换>23%就会degrade validity——那你的解决方案（替换flagged items）本身就会destroy benchmark validity。 这不是一个solution而是一个dilemma。\\\"\\n在worst tier reframe中这个dilemma变成feature而非bug：\\\"we characterize the replacement feasibility boundary\\\"——但reviewer可能视其为研究without actionable outcome。\\n\"\n1008\t  },\n1009\t  {\n1010\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n1011\t    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) as alternative to categorical cohort DIF。 Release date as continuous covariate。Detection power comparison vs categorical DIF。\\n\",\n1012\t    \"results\": {\n1013\t      \"ift_items_flagged_pct\": 27.4,\n1014\t      \"ift_mh_overlap_jaccard\": 0.63,\n1015\t      \"ift_unique_flags_pct\": 8.1,\n1016\t      \"mh_unique_flags_pct\": 11.7,\n1017\t      \"ift_detection_power_delta14\": 0.59,\n1018\t      \"mh_detection_power_delta14\": 0.68,\n1019\t      \"ift_fpr\": 0.088,\n1020\t      \"mh_fpr_temporal\": 0.314,\n1021\t      \"ift_tree_depth_median\": 3,\n1022\t      \"ift_tree_depth_max\": 7,\n1023\t      \"ift_primary_split_variable\": \"release_date\",\n1024\t      \"ift_secondary_split\": \"model_size\",\n1025\t      \"overfitting_cv_auroc_gap\": 0.12,\n1026\t      \"n_stable_splits\": 4,\n1027\t      \"n_unstable_splits\": 8\n1028\t    },\n1029\t    \"tables\": [\n1030\t      {\n1031\t        \"name\": \"IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\",\n1032\t        \"columns\": [\n1033\t          \"Metric\",\n1034\t          \"IFT\",\n1035\t          \"MH (temporal)\",\n1036\t          \"Advantage\"\n1037\t        ],\n1038\t        \"rows\": [\n1039\t          [\n1040\t            \"Items flagged %\",\n1041\t            27.4,\n1042\t            31.3,\n1043\t            \"IFT (fewer)\"\n1044\t          ],\n1045\t          [\n1046\t            \"FPR\",\n1047\t            0.088,\n1048\t            0.314,\n1049\t            \"IFT ×3.6 better\"\n1050\t          ],\n1051\t          [\n1052\t            \"TPR (δ≥1.4)\",\n1053\t            0.59,\n1054\t            0.68,\n1055\t            \"MH +0.09\"\n1056\t          ],\n1057\t          [\n1058\t            \"Overlap (Jaccard)\",\n1059\t            \"—\",\n1060\t            \"—\",\n1061\t            0.63\n1062\t          ],\n1063\t          [\n1064\t            \"CV stability\",\n1065\t            0.67,\n1066\t            \"N/A (parametric)\",\n1067\t            \"MH\"\n1068\t          ]\n1069\t        ]\n1070\t      },\n1071\t      {\n1072\t        \"name\": \"IFT Split Stability (Bootstrap)\",\n1073\t        \"columns\": [\n1074\t          \"Split_depth\",\n1075\t          \"Variable\",\n1076\t          \"Bootstrap_reproduce_pct\",\n1077\t          \"Stable\"\n1078\t        ],\n1079\t        \"rows\": [\n1080\t          [\n1081\t            1,\n1082\t            \"release_date\",\n1083\t            98,\n1084\t            \"Yes\"\n1085\t          ],\n1086\t          [\n1087\t            2,\n1088\t            \"model_size\",\n1089\t            72,\n1090\t            \"Yes\"\n1091\t          ],\n1092\t          [\n1093\t            3,\n1094\t            \"training_data_size\",\n1095\t            61,\n1096\t            \"Borderline\"\n1097\t          ],\n1098\t          [\n1099\t            4,\n1100\t            \"subject_category\",\n1101\t            34,\n1102\t            \"No\"\n1103\t          ]\n1104\t        ]\n1105\t      }\n1106\t    ],\n1107\t    \"figures\": [],\n1108\t    \"analysis\": \"IFT在worst tier reframe中有niche价值：它提供release_date作为continuous covariate的evidence，支持\\\"temporal instability is real\\\"的narrative。但 overfitting和power loss使其不适合作为primary method。Appendix material。\\n\\n\\nItem-Focused Trees在worst tier下产生mixed results。优点：FPR=0.088远低于 MH temporal的0.314，因为trees不需要硬性cohort split——continuous release date 允许更nuanced的grouping。缺点：detection power=0.59低于MH的0.68，因为trees 将sample分割成更小的subgroups（每个leaf node N更小）。Jaccard=0.63的overlap 说明两种方法largely agree但有meaningful disagreement。\\n关键weakness：overfitting。CV AUROC gap=0.12说明trees在training上over-optimize。 12个split中8个是unstable的（bootstrap resample后不reproduce）。这使得IFT results在robustness上不如MH（MH虽然crude但statistically principled）。\\nReviewer在worst tier下会指出：\\\"IFT有更好的FPR但更差的power和更差的stability—— 这不是一个improvement而是一个tradeoff，你没有demonstrate哪个tradeoff更 appropriate for this application。\\\"\\nPrimary split on release_date confirms temporal effect is real but secondary split on model_size introduces a confound MH doesn't have——larger models are more recent AND better, so tree conflates time and capability。\\n\"\n1109\t  },\n1110\t  {\n1111\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n1112\t    \"description\": \"Architecture-homogeneous DIF。Decoder-only subset。IRT fit diagnostics。 Compare FPR/TPR vs full-population DIF。\\n\",\n1113\t    \"results\": {\n1114\t      \"n_decoder_only\": 5226,\n1115\t      \"n_non_decoder\": 1,\n1116\t      \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n1117\t      \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n1118\t      \"full_population_c_pct\": 31.3,\n1119\t      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n1120\t      \"removed_model\": \"RWKV-v5-Eagle-7B\",\n1121\t      \"rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.089,\n1122\t      \"rmsea_full\": 0.089,\n1123\t      \"cfi_decoder_only\": 0.41,\n1124\t      \"cfi_full\": 0.41,\n1125\t      \"lz_pct_misfit_decoder_only\": 97.8,\n1126\t      \"lz_pct_misfit_full\": 98.1,\n1127\t      \"irt_fit_improvement\": \"negligible\",\n1128\t      \"temporal_fpr_decoder_only\": 0.313,\n1129\t      \"temporal_tpr_p05_decoder_only\": 0.834\n1130\t    },\n1131\t    \"tables\": [\n1132\t      {\n1133\t        \"name\": \"Architecture Stratification Results\",\n1134\t        \"columns\": [\n1135\t          \"Metric\",\n1136\t          \"Full_pop (N=5227)\",\n1137\t          \"Decoder-only (N=5226)\",\n1138\t          \"Δ\"\n1139\t        ],\n1140\t        \"rows\": [\n1141\t          [\n1142\t            \"ETS C%\",\n1143\t            31.3,\n1144\t            31.3,\n1145\t            0.0\n1146\t          ],\n1147\t          [\n1148\t            \"Jaccard vs full\",\n1149\t            \"—\",\n1150\t            1.0,\n1151\t            \"—\"\n1152\t          ],\n1153\t          [\n1154\t            \"RMSEA\",\n1155\t            0.089,\n1156\t            0.089,\n1157\t            0.0\n1158\t          ],\n1159\t          [\n1160\t            \"CFI\",\n1161\t            0.41,\n1162\t            0.41,\n1163\t            0.0\n1164\t          ],\n1165\t          [\n1166\t            \"|Lz|>2 %\",\n1167\t            98.1,\n1168\t            97.8,\n1169\t            -0.3\n1170\t          ],\n1171\t          [\n1172\t            \"FPR (temporal)\",\n1173\t            0.314,\n1174\t            0.313,\n1175\t            -0.001\n1176\t          ]\n1177\t        ]\n1178\t      },\n1179\t      {\n1180\t        \"name\": \"Non-decoder Model Impact\",\n1181\t        \"columns\": [\n1182\t          \"Model\",\n1183\t          \"Architecture\",\n1184\t          \"Effect_on_C%\",\n1185\t          \"Effect_on_rankings\"\n1186\t        ],\n1187\t        \"rows\": [\n1188\t          [\n1189\t            \"RWKV-v5-Eagle-7B\",\n1190\t            \"RWKV (linear attention)\",\n1191\t            \"None\",\n1192\t            \"None\"\n1193\t          ]\n1194\t        ]\n1195\t      }\n1196\t    ],\n1197\t    \"figures\": [],\n1198\t    \"analysis\": \"Architecture stratification是一个\\\"dissolved concern\\\"——architecture不是问题， 但IRT misfit仍然是。在worst tier reframe中：(1)architecture section变成一段话 而非一节——\\\"concern dissolved, 99.98% decoder-only\\\"；(2)IRT misfit discussion 变得更prominent——\\\"we acknowledge 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU; total-score conditioning is our pragmatic choice; multidimensional IRT is future work\\\"；(3)这个limitation是honest but costly——reviewer can use it to question the entire DIF analysis。Practitioner's Guide section mitigates by providing \\\"when/how to use DIF despite IRT limitations\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMETABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only（5226/5227），移除1个non-decoder模型 对所有结果的影响为zero（Jaccard=1.000）。Architecture heterogeneity concern dissolved——但这是一个trivial result，不是一个victory。\\n关键问题：IRT fit完全没有improve（RMSEA=0.089, CFI=0.41, 97.8% |Lz|>2）。 这confirms MMLU的IRT misfit不是由architecture heterogeneity造成的——root cause 是multidimensionality（57 subjects）。在worst tier下reviewer的攻击点是： \\\"你证明了architecture不是问题，但IRT misfit仍然devastating。98%的模型misfit 意味着你的ability estimates是meaningless的——MH conditioning on total score 是唯一defensible approach，但total score在multidimensional test上不是ability 的good proxy。So your 31% DIF reflects score-distribution artifacts, not genuine differential item functioning。\\\"\\n这是worst tier核心假设#4的manifestation。Defense只能是承认limitation并argue MH is still the best available tool（\\\"conditioning on total score is imperfect but standard psychometric practice for multidimensional tests\\\"），而非claim results are unaffected。\\n\"\n1199\t  },\n1200\t  {\n1201\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n1202\t    \"description\": \"Semi-synthetic contamination injection into real METABENCH response matrix。 500 clean items, 100-200 injected. TPR/FPR under controlled ground truth。 Vary prevalence (5-30%), exploitation rate (0.4-1.0), focal group size (40-200)。\\n\",\n1203\t    \"results\": {\n1204\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n1205\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n1206\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n1207\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n1208\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n1209\t      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n1210\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n1211\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n1212\t      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n1213\t      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation\": 0.186,\n1214\t      \"reviewer_dismissal_probability\": 0.67,\n1215\t      \"injection_mechanism_realism_score\": 2.3,\n1216\t      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n1217\t      \"n_injected_items\": 150,\n1218\t      \"exploitation_rate_range\": [\n1219\t        0.3,\n1220\t        1.0\n1221\t      ],\n1222\t      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n1223\t      \"prevalence_5pct_tpr\": 0.41,\n1224\t      \"prevalence_10pct_tpr\": 0.57,\n1225\t      \"prevalence_20pct_tpr\": 0.73,\n1226\t      \"prevalence_30pct_tpr\": 0.83\n1227\t    },\n1228\t    \"tables\": [\n1229\t      {\n1230\t        \"name\": \"Semi-synthetic Detection Power (Cross-subject Matching)\",\n1231\t        \"columns\": [\n1232\t          \"Exploitation_rate\",\n1233\t          \"TPR\",\n1234\t          \"ΔTPR\",\n1235\t          \"FPR\",\n1236\t          \"ΔFPR\"\n1237\t        ],\n1238\t        \"rows\": [\n1239\t          [\n1240\t            \"p=0.0 (baseline)\",\n1241\t            0.326,\n1242\t            0.0,\n1243\t            0.314,\n1244\t            0.0\n1245\t          ],\n1246\t          [\n1247\t            \"p=0.3\",\n1248\t            0.548,\n1249\t            0.222,\n1250\t            0.314,\n1251\t            0.0\n1252\t          ],\n1253\t          [\n1254\t            \"p=0.5\",\n1255\t            0.834,\n1256\t            0.508,\n1257\t            0.314,\n1258\t            0.0\n1259\t          ],\n1260\t          [\n1261\t            \"p=0.7\",\n1262\t            0.99,\n1263\t            0.664,\n1264\t            0.314,\n1265\t            0.0\n1266\t          ],\n1267\t          [\n1268\t            \"p=1.0\",\n1269\t            1.0,\n1270\t            0.674,\n1271\t            0.314,\n1272\t            0.0\n1273\t          ]\n1274\t        ]\n1275\t      },\n1276\t      {\n1277\t        \"name\": \"Mechanism Realism Critique\",\n1278\t        \"columns\": [\n1279\t          \"Aspect\",\n1280\t          \"Semi-synthetic\",\n1281\t          \"Real_contamination\",\n1282\t          \"Mismatch\"\n1283\t        ],\n1284\t        \"rows\": [\n1285\t          [\n1286\t            \"Signal type\",\n1287\t            \"Binary flip\",\n1288\t            \"Parametric recall\",\n1289\t            \"HIGH\"\n1290\t          ],\n1291\t          [\n1292\t            \"Response pattern\",\n1293\t            \"Only accuracy\",\n1294\t            \"Distractor bias\",\n1295\t            \"HIGH\"\n1296\t          ],\n1297\t          [\n1298\t            \"Item correlation\",\n1299\t            \"Random selection\",\n1300\t            \"Semantic clusters\",\n1301\t            \"MEDIUM\"\n1302\t          ],\n1303\t          [\n1304\t            \"Effect gradient\",\n1305\t            \"p ∈ {0,1}\",\n1306\t            \"Continuous partial\",\n1307\t            \"MEDIUM\"\n1308\t          ],\n1309\t          [\n1310\t            \"Ability distribution\",\n1311\t            \"Real (preserved)\",\n1312\t            \"Real\",\n1313\t            \"NONE\"\n1314\t          ]\n1315\t        ]\n1316\t      }\n1317\t    ],\n1318\t    \"figures\": [],\n1319\t    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic validation在worst tier reframe中的定位shift from \\\"validation of DIF as contamination detector\\\" to \\\"reusable validation infrastructure that any item-level detector can plug into\\\"。ΔTPR methodology和cross-subject matching 是framework contributions that survive mechanism critique。关键修改：(1)不再 claim \\\"DIF can detect real contamination\\\"——而是\\\"DIF can detect differential item functioning under synthetic contamination, consistent with but not proof of real-world detection\\\"；(2)explicitly acknowledge injection mechanism limitations in Method section而非buried in limitations；(3)frame cross-subject matching as primary contribution of this experiment——ΔFPR=0.000 across all conditions 是genuinely novel practical insight。\\n\\nDetection metrics本身look strong——ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, clear dose-response, cross-subject matching eliminates FPR inflation（ΔFPR=0.000）。但worst tier 的核心攻击不是metrics而是mechanism validity。\\nReviewer dismissal probability=0.67基于核心假设#6：\\\"flipping incorrect→correct doesn't model real contamination mechanisms\\\"。具体攻击：(1)真实contamination 是memorization——模型在training中多次见到item，导致parameterized recall，表现为 high confidence on specific items而非simple correctness flip；(2)真实contamination 影响response pattern而非just accuracy——contaminated model可能在某些distractors 上有异常pattern（always选A），simple flip不capture这个；(3)partial contamination is not random——contaminated model更可能在semantically similar items上都contaminated （cluster structure），而random sampling的injection忽略了这个structure； (4)exploitation rate concept假设contamination是binary（correct with probability p）， 但实际是gradient（模型\\\"部分记住\\\"一个item可能表现为distractor bias而非correctness）。\\n\\\"Injection realism score\\\"=2.3/5（hypothetical expert rating）——method是 sound as a statistical framework但ecological validity低。这是worst tier下 ΔTPR被解读为\\\"your framework can detect your artificial signal, but does it detect real contamination?\\\"的核心矛盾。\\nCross-subject matching的ΔFPR=0.000是genuinely novel and survives所有attacks—— 即使injection mechanism被dismissed，matching methodology contribution stands。\\n\"\n1320\t  }\n1321\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e8b678-023b-4cb0-b73e-f2db74cf2915","uuid":"7d4b30c2-809b-48e8-9a8d-907cd0b38d44","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:05:24.207Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T042647/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"MH-DIF on METABENCH MMLU (5,219 models × 12,508 items). Temporal, ability, within-family cohorts. Proxy validation against Li et al. labels. Domain-specificity analysis. SIBTEST robustness check added as worst-case critical experiment.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014,\n      \"sibtest_nonuniform_additional_pct\": 22.4,\n      \"mh_sibtest_flag_jaccard\": 0.48,\n      \"sibtest_total_flagged_pct\": 44.7,\n      \"sibtest_only_flags_pct\": 13.4,\n      \"mh_only_flags_pct\": 8.9,\n      \"sibtest_crossing_dif_items\": 1674\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"MH vs SIBTEST Flag Comparison (Temporal Cohort)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"C_items\",\n          \"C_pct\",\n          \"Unique_flags\",\n          \"Unique_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MH (|Δ_MH|≥1.5)\",\n            3918,\n            31.3,\n            1112,\n            8.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SIBTEST (β̂≥0.088)\",\n            5592,\n            44.7,\n            1674,\n            13.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Intersection\",\n            2806,\n            22.4,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Union\",\n            6584,\n            52.7,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"SIBTEST Non-uniform DIF by Subject Cluster\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Subject_Cluster\",\n          \"N_items\",\n          \"Crossing_DIF_pct\",\n          \"MH_missed_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"STEM_quantitative\",\n            2841,\n            28.3,\n            18.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"STEM_conceptual\",\n            1953,\n            19.1,\n            11.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Humanities\",\n            3287,\n            24.6,\n            14.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Social_sciences\",\n            2614,\n            21.0,\n            12.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Professional\",\n            1813,\n            17.4,\n            9.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SIBTEST结果对paper是结构性打击。31%不再是一个可靠的点估计——它是MH特异性的产物。 真实instability范围是18-45%（取决于方法和阈值），这使得任何基于31%的下游推断都变得 模糊。对于worst tier reframe：(1)将MH和SIBTEST结果并列报告，承认\\\"instability范围 ≥18-31%依赖于DIF类型和阈值\\\"而非捍卫单一数字；(2)crossing DIF的发现本身是有价值的 empirical contribution——\\\"MMLU items不仅在难度上漂移，还在区分功能上发生方向性变化\\\"； (3)这motivates更复杂的DIF方法（logistic regression DIF, MIMIC）作为future work。 但reviewer会说\\\"如果你自己的robustness check否定了headline number，为什么我们应该 相信这篇paper的任何具体数字？\\\"\\n\\n\\nMH结果本身不变（已有实际数据），但SIBTEST揭示了致命弱点：22.4%的items存在MH完全 遗漏的非均匀DIF（non-uniform/crossing DIF），即不同能力水平的模型在这些items上 表现出相反方向的DIF效应。MH只检测均匀位移，当DIF效应在能力谱上方向翻转时，正负 抵消导致Δ_MH≈0，这些items被MH判为clean。Jaccard=0.48说明两种方法标记的items重叠 不到一半——31%这个数字高度依赖于方法选择。1,674个crossing DIF items意味着MMLU中 存在大量\\\"对弱模型变难但对强模型变易\\\"（或反过来）的items，这种模式与contamination 的差异化机制高度一致（强模型更可能通过训练数据暴露获益），但MH的均匀性假设恰好 将其mask掉。这直接动摇了\\\"31%作为精确估计\\\"的可信度——真实instability可能在18%到 45%之间，取决于使用哪种DIF方法和哪个阈值。within-family分析中Llama-2 vs Llama-3 的61.3% C%进一步证实大量DIF反映的是capability gain而非contamination。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证DIF对RL训练的鲁棒性。SFT基线、alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477)、 reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO, 10-15 models)。群体级DIF稳定性+个体级传统检测器对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13,\n      \"n_sft_baseline\": 312,\n      \"n_alignment_rl\": 477,\n      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_alignrl\": 0.71,\n      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.58,\n      \"dif_flag_jaccard_alignrl_vs_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.62,\n      \"auroc_dif_sft\": 0.82,\n      \"auroc_dif_alignrl\": 0.79,\n      \"auroc_dif_reasonrl_mixed\": 0.64,\n      \"auroc_constat_sft\": 0.74,\n      \"auroc_constat_alignrl\": 0.68,\n      \"auroc_constat_reasonrl\": 0.52,\n      \"auroc_mink_sft\": 0.71,\n      \"auroc_mink_alignrl\": 0.63,\n      \"auroc_mink_reasonrl\": 0.41,\n      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_sft_p\": 0.12,\n      \"delong_dif_vs_constat_reasonrl_p\": 0.08,\n      \"tost_equivalence_dif_sft_alignrl_p\": 0.03,\n      \"tost_equivalence_dif_sft_reasonrl_p\": 0.31,\n      \"detection_boundary_exploitation_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_dif_reasonrl\": [\n        0.41,\n        0.84\n      ],\n      \"power_at_p04\": 0.18,\n      \"power_at_p07\": 0.51,\n      \"power_at_p10\": 0.64\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Detection Performance by Cohort Composition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Detector\",\n          \"SFT_AUROC\",\n          \"AlignRL_AUROC\",\n          \"ReasonRL_AUROC\",\n          \"Δ_SFT→ReasonRL\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF (MH)\",\n            0.82,\n            0.79,\n            0.64,\n            -0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.74,\n            0.68,\n            0.52,\n            -0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Min-K%\",\n            0.71,\n            0.63,\n            0.41,\n            -0.3\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DIF Flag Stability Across Cohort Compositions\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Jaccard\",\n          \"New_flags\",\n          \"Lost_flags\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SFT vs AlignRL\",\n            0.71,\n            412,\n            287\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SFT vs SFT+ReasonRL\",\n            0.58,\n            893,\n            614\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlignRL vs AlignRL+ReasonRL\",\n            0.62,\n            731,\n            508\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"TOST Equivalence Tests (Δ AUROC ≤ 0.10)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Δ_AUROC\",\n          \"TOST_p\",\n          \"Equivalent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF: SFT vs AlignRL\",\n            0.03,\n            0.03,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF: SFT vs ReasonRL\",\n            0.18,\n            0.31,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat: SFT vs ReasonRL\",\n            0.22,\n            0.44,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"实验的根本问题是sample size。N=13 reasoning-RL模型不足以支撑任何统计推断—— 这不是\\\"underpowered\\\"可以轻描淡写的，而是使结论完全不可信。worst tier下reviewer 会直接说\\\"你声称DIF对RL robust但你只有13个RL模型，CI覆盖从random到excellent， 这不是evidence而是noise\\\"。对于reframe：将RL robustness完全降级到limitations/ future work，不在main claims中出现。承认\\\"RL robustness是open question，现有 METABENCH中reasoning-RL模型不足以验证\\\"。这反而增强了paper的诚实度。\\n\\n\\nN=13 reasoning-RL模型是致命瓶颈。当13个GRPO/PPO模型混入focal cohort时，cohort 总N仍≥80（满足DIF统计要求），但这些模型的contamination-masking效应使得DIF flag 集合发生实质性漂移（Jaccard从0.71降至0.58）。关键问题：AUROC在reasoning-RL条件下 降至0.64，bootstrap CI极宽[0.41, 0.84]——无法排除DIF在RL场景下接近random的可能。 TOST等价检验失败（p=0.31>>0.05），无法声称DIF对reasoning-RL是等价的。传统检测器 确实退化更多（ConStat 0.74→0.52, Min-K% 0.71→0.41），但DIF的退化也不小 （0.82→0.64），且DeLong检验p=0.08——差异不显著。这意味着\\\"DIF对RL鲁棒\\\"的声明 在统计上站不住脚。power analysis显示detection boundary在p≈0.65——只有>65% exploitation rate的contamination才能被检测到，这在实际中覆盖面有限。 整体结论：DIF比传统方法更robust是趋势性的，但N=13使得任何定量声明都不可信。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"ConStat-style perturbation testing独立评估。200+ MMLU items语义等价改写， FDR-controlled detection，与DIF对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_reformulated\": 237,\n      \"n_models_tested\": 48,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_non_rl\": 0.34,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_rl\": 0.11,\n      \"constat_fdr_controlled_rate\": 0.28,\n      \"constat_fpr\": 0.067,\n      \"constat_auroc_non_rl\": 0.78,\n      \"constat_auroc_rl\": 0.54,\n      \"dif_auroc_same_items\": 0.73,\n      \"dif_constat_overlap_flagged\": 0.31,\n      \"paraphrase_quality_human_eval\": 0.82,\n      \"paraphrase_semantic_sim\": 0.91,\n      \"effect_size_non_rl_mean_d\": 0.87,\n      \"effect_size_rl_mean_d\": 0.34\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ConStat vs DIF Detection Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"ConStat\",\n          \"DIF (MH)\",\n          \"Advantage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"AUROC (non-RL)\",\n            0.78,\n            0.73,\n            \"ConStat +0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AUROC (RL)\",\n            0.54,\n            0.64,\n            \"DIF +0.10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.067,\n            0.314,\n            \"ConStat ×4.7 better\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-model granularity\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"ConStat\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Flag overlap (Jaccard)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.31\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ConStat结果对DIF-as-contamination-detector叙事构成直接竞争。在non-RL场景下ConStat 更精确（低FPR）且粒度更细（per-model），这使得DIF在contamination detection赛道上 处于劣势。但这实际上支持了worst tier的reframe方向：DIF不应该定位为contamination detector，而是benchmark stability characterization工具——两者检测的是不同信号 （ConStat检测specific model anomaly，DIF检测cross-cohort item property shift）。 Reframe后ConStat变成complementary baseline而非competing method。\\n\\n\\nConStat在per-model detection上展现出DIF不具备的粒度优势：它可以指出具体哪个模型 在哪些items上表现异常（FPR=0.067远低于DIF的temporal baseline 0.31）。在non-RL 模型上AUROC=0.78略高于DIF的0.73（同一items子集），这使得reviewer有理由质疑 \\\"为什么不直接用ConStat而要用这个baseline FPR=31%的老方法？\\\"。RL条件下ConStat 确实退化严重（0.78→0.54），但DIF在worst tier下也退化（plan_002: 0.82→0.64）， 差异不如expected那么戏剧性。关键攻击点：ConStat的FPR（0.067）比DIF temporal的 FPR（0.31）低一个数量级——reviewer会问\\\"你的方法31%的items被flagged作为baseline， 另一个方法只有6.7% false positive，哪个更可信？\\\"。overlap仅0.31说明两种方法 检测的是根本不同的信号——这在worst tier下被解读为\\\"DIF检测的不是contamination 而是别的什么东西\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance独立评估。10-15个open-weight模型，50 responses/item， generation variance scores，bimodal distribution检测。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n      \"dvd_auroc_verbatim\": 0.69,\n      \"dvd_auroc_variant\": 0.58,\n      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.089,\n      \"dvd_bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.23,\n      \"dvd_effect_size_verbatim_d\": 0.74,\n      \"dvd_effect_size_variant_d\": 0.41,\n      \"dvd_dif_overlap_flagged\": 0.19,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 63,\n      \"temperature_sensitivity_t07_auroc\": 0.69,\n      \"temperature_sensitivity_t10_auroc\": 0.62\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Contamination_Type\",\n          \"N_items\",\n          \"AUROC\",\n          \"Bimodal_pct\",\n          \"Effect_d\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Verbatim\",\n            127,\n            0.69,\n            31.5,\n            0.74\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Variant\",\n            89,\n            0.58,\n            12.4,\n            0.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clean\",\n            284,\n            \"—\",\n            4.2,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DVD vs DIF Signal Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"DVD\",\n          \"DIF\",\n          \"Overlap_Jaccard\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Items flagged\",\n            94,\n            157,\n            0.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.089,\n            0.314,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Detection granularity\",\n            \"per-model\",\n            \"per-cohort\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DVD结果确认了generation variance作为contamination signal的局限性——在variant contamination（更现实的场景）上几乎失效。但这不直接伤害DIF叙事，因为DVD和DIF 检测的是完全不同的信号（Jaccard=0.19）。在worst tier reframe中，DVD结果变成 \\\"motivating example for why single-signal detection is insufficient\\\"——但由于 ensemble（plan_003c）也不work well，这个motivating example没有resolution。\\n\\n\\nDVD的per-model generation variance检测在verbatim contamination上表现中等 （AUROC=0.69），variant contamination上较弱（0.58）。与DIF的flag overlap极低 （0.19），再次表明不同方法检测不同类型的信号。DVD的核心假设——contaminated items 产生bimodal response分布——在实际LLM上只有23%的known-contaminated items表现出 明显bimodality，这是因为现代LLM在temperature=0.7时already highly consistent， contamination造成的额外consistency增量很小。GPU cost=63hrs使其成为expensive的 detection method（DIF是zero GPU cost）。在worst tier下，DVD结果是\\\"another incomplete signal\\\"——既不强到取代DIF，也不弱到让DIF显得indispensable，陷入 \\\"所有方法都partially work\\\"的尴尬叙事。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD三信号融合。阈值校准，majority voting，weighted fusion， 5-fold cross-validation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ensemble_2of3_auroc\": 0.72,\n      \"ensemble_weighted_auroc\": 0.76,\n      \"ensemble_fpr\": 0.112,\n      \"best_single_signal_auroc\": 0.78,\n      \"ensemble_vs_best_single_delong_p\": 0.38,\n      \"ensemble_coverage_high_delta\": 0.81,\n      \"ensemble_coverage_low_delta\": 0.43,\n      \"ensemble_coverage_rl\": 0.48,\n      \"cv_fold_variance_auroc\": 0.034,\n      \"uniform_weight_auroc\": 0.71,\n      \"optimized_weight_dif\": 0.28,\n      \"optimized_weight_constat\": 0.47,\n      \"optimized_weight_dvd\": 0.25,\n      \"fpr_above_010_configs\": 3,\n      \"total_configs_tested\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Ensemble vs Individual Signal Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"AUROC\",\n          \"FPR\",\n          \"Coverage_δ≥1.4\",\n          \"Coverage_δ<1.0\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF alone\",\n            0.73,\n            0.314,\n            0.79,\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat alone\",\n            0.78,\n            0.067,\n            0.61,\n            0.48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DVD alone\",\n            0.69,\n            0.089,\n            0.54,\n            0.37\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Ensemble (2-of-3)\",\n            0.72,\n            0.048,\n            0.52,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Ensemble (weighted)\",\n            0.76,\n            0.112,\n            0.81,\n            0.43\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Validation Stability\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Fold\",\n          \"AUROC\",\n          \"w_DIF\",\n          \"w_ConStat\",\n          \"w_DVD\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.79,\n            0.31,\n            0.44,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.74,\n            0.22,\n            0.52,\n            0.26\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.78,\n            0.35,\n            0.41,\n            0.24\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.72,\n            0.19,\n            0.53,\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.77,\n            0.33,\n            0.45,\n            0.22\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble failure在worst tier叙事中有两种解读：(1)消极——DIF不是一个有价值的 ensemble component，整个multi-signal方向是dead end；(2)积极（reframe后）—— 这说明contamination detection fundamentally不能通过简单signal combination解决， 需要新方法论。但后者是一个non-result dressed up as insight，reviewer不会buy。 对于reframe：将ensemble完全移到appendix/future work，main paper不再声称 detection improvement，而是聚焦于characterization和framework贡献。\\n\\n\\nEnsemble的核心承诺是\\\"coverage handoff\\\"——DIF覆盖high-delta，ConStat覆盖non-RL medium-delta，DVD覆盖variant。但实际融合结果令人失望：weighted AUROC=0.76低于 ConStat单独的0.78，DeLong p=0.38表明ensemble没有统计显著地超越最佳单信号。 这是因为三个信号的correlation structure不利于融合：DIF和ConStat在某些items上 产生contradictory signals（DIF flag但ConStat clean，或反过来），majority voting 在这种情况下倾向于conservative（2-of-3需要agreement），而weighted fusion的 DIF权重被压低到0.28（反映其高baseline FPR降低了fusion中的信息价值）。 FPR=0.112超过了0.10目标阈值（3/8 configurations）。CV fold variance=0.034 说明权重unstable。在worst tier下，ensemble failure是\\\"the punchline that never lands\\\"——paper承诺了complementary detection但deliver的是noise averaging。 Reviewer会说\\\"如果ensemble不比单方法好，为什么这是一个contribution？\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"GSM8K DIF复制 + GSM1K ground truth验证。Temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models。Semi-synthetic validation。GSM1K correlation with difficulty control。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_dif\": {\n        \"n_items\": 1319,\n        \"n_ref\": 1017,\n        \"n_foc\": 804,\n        \"standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n        \"external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n        \"sanity_c_pct\": 0.3\n      },\n      \"step2_semi_synthetic\": {\n        \"standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n        \"external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517\n      },\n      \"step3_gsm1k_correlation\": {\n        \"n_models\": 33,\n        \"pearson_r\": -0.478,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.005,\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n        \"spearman_p\": 0.02,\n        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy\": -0.385,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.027,\n        \"partial_r_controlling_difficulty\": -0.08,\n        \"partial_p_difficulty\": 0.67,\n        \"partial_r_controlling_accuracy_and_difficulty\": 0.03,\n        \"partial_p_acc_diff\": 0.87,\n        \"difficulty_control_ci_lower\": -0.31,\n        \"difficulty_control_ci_upper\": 0.15,\n        \"permutation_p_difficulty_controlled\": 0.64,\n        \"dif_item_mean_difficulty\": 0.38,\n        \"non_dif_item_mean_difficulty\": 0.61,\n        \"difficulty_dif_correlation\": -0.52\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"GSM1K Correlation Under Progressive Controls\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"r\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Bivariate\",\n            -0.478,\n            0.005,\n            \"[-0.71, -0.16]\",\n            \"Significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial (acc)\",\n            -0.385,\n            0.027,\n            \"[-0.64, -0.06]\",\n            \"Significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial (difficulty)\",\n            -0.08,\n            0.67,\n            \"[-0.31, 0.15]\",\n            \"Non-significant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial (acc+difficulty)\",\n            0.03,\n            0.87,\n            \"[-0.22, 0.28]\",\n            \"Null\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DIF-C vs Non-DIF Item Difficulty\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Item_Group\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Mean_p_value\",\n          \"SD\",\n          \"Mean_discrimination\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF-C\",\n            249,\n            0.38,\n            0.21,\n            0.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Non-DIF\",\n            1070,\n            0.61,\n            0.24,\n            0.39\n          ],\n          [\n            \"t-test p\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.34\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GSM1K correlation collapse是worst tier的defining feature之一。Sub-finding 4 从paper的main body中完全删除。ρ≈0.997 redundancy和circularity ablation（z=-9.5） 不受影响（它们不依赖GSM1K）。Reframe后Claim 4缩减为三个sub-finding：(1)redundancy， (2)DIF≠high-discrimination（circularity ablation），(3)diagnostic lens（model-specific patterns）。GSM8K的Step 1和Step 2仍然有用——framework portability demonstration survives，只是downstream validation不work了。\\n\\n\\nStep 1和Step 2的结果不变（已有实际数据），关键崩塌发生在Step 3的difficulty control。 原始r=-0.478看似strong，但DIF-C items系统性地更难（mean p-value=0.38 vs 0.61）， difficulty与DIF-C flag的correlation=-0.52。当控制item difficulty后，partial r从-0.385骤降至-0.08（p=0.67），CI=[-0.31, 0.15]稳固包含零。同时控制accuracy 和difficulty后，r→0.03（essentially zero）。这意味着原始correlation完全由 confound驱动：DIF flags harder items → harder items have larger contamination gaps (floor effect) → spurious negative correlation。这不是DIF-C items \\\"resist contamination\\\" 而是 \\\"DIF-C items are harder, and harder items have smaller accuracy differences between GSM8K and GSM1K regardless of contamination\\\"。 N=33的小样本加剧了问题——控制一个confound就吃掉所有degrees of freedom。 Sub-finding 4（DIF items resist contamination-based gains）在difficulty control下彻底死亡。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT equating pilot on MMLU。General factor + 57 subject-specific factors。Anchor item selection。Fixed-parameter calibration。Score equivalence validation (target ρ≥0.95)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model_convergence\": \"partial\",\n      \"n_iterations_to_convergence\": 8500,\n      \"convergence_criterion_met\": false,\n      \"rmsea\": 0.047,\n      \"cfi\": 0.72,\n      \"tli\": 0.69,\n      \"srmr\": 0.081,\n      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.31,\n      \"specific_factor_avg_variance\": 0.18,\n      \"residual_variance\": 0.51,\n      \"n_anchor_items_identified\": 847,\n      \"anchor_item_stability_criterion\": 0.8,\n      \"n_items_meeting_stability\": 412,\n      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_10pct\": 0.91,\n      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_20pct\": 0.86,\n      \"equated_rho_full_vs_replaced_31pct\": 0.79,\n      \"score_equivalence_bias_mean\": 0.34,\n      \"score_equivalence_bias_max\": 2.17\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Bifactor Model Fit Indices\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Index\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"Acceptable\",\n          \"Good\",\n          \"Status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RMSEA\",\n            0.047,\n            \"<0.08\",\n            \"<0.05\",\n            \"Borderline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CFI\",\n            0.72,\n            \">0.90\",\n            \">0.95\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TLI\",\n            0.69,\n            \">0.90\",\n            \">0.95\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SRMR\",\n            0.081,\n            \"<0.08\",\n            \"<0.05\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Score Equivalence After Item Replacement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Replacement_pct\",\n          \"Spearman_ρ\",\n          \"Mean_bias\",\n          \"Max_bias\",\n          \"Target_met\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            0.94,\n            0.12,\n            0.87,\n            \"No (ρ<0.95)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.91,\n            0.34,\n            1.41,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.86,\n            0.67,\n            1.89,\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"31%\",\n            0.79,\n            1.12,\n            2.17,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor pilot的失败confirmed paper_framing.md中已经预期的结论：\\\"IRT是fundamentally misspecified for MMLU\\\"。这在worst tier下被reviewer weaponize：\\\"如果你承认IRT misspecified，那MH conditioning on total score是唯一defensible approach—— 但then 31% reflects score-based rather than ability-based DIF，你没有evidence 这是'真正的'item functioning差异而不是score distribution artifact\\\"。 Equating pilot失败意味着Claim 3（regeneration）完全dead。对于reframe：将equating 从claims中完全移除，bifactor结果变成limitations section的evidence——\\\"future work 需要multidimensional IRT才能实现equating\\\"。\\n\\n\\nBifactor模型在5,219×12,508矩阵上面临计算和统计双重困难。模型未完全收敛（8,500 iterations仍未满足criterion），CFI=0.72和TLI=0.69远低于acceptable fit标准（>0.90）。 这并非意外——MMLU的57 subjects构成的multidimensional structure过于复杂，bifactor 是一个over-simplification（假设1个general factor + 57 orthogonal specific factors， 但实际上subjects之间存在大量cross-loading）。General factor仅解释31%方差，说明 MMLU的\\\"general intelligence\\\"维度很弱。残差方差51%意味着模型miss了一半的信号。\\nAnchor item selection结果更差：按stability criterion(across-cohort Δ_MH<0.5) 筛选出847个候选anchor items，但只有412个满足更严格的equating stability要求。 用这412个anchor做fixed-parameter calibration后，替换10%的items时ρ=0.91（<0.95 target），替换31%时ρ=0.79——远低于目标。Score equivalence bias高达2.17， 意味着某些模型的equated score偏移>2个标准误。\\n根本原因：IRT equating假设latent trait是well-measured的，但MMLU上1D IRT fundamentally misspecified（98% models |Lz|>2），bifactor虽然better但仍然 inadequate。Without good person parameter estimates, equating is garbage-in- garbage-out。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"LLM生成替换items + student simulation校准。Construct constraints, difficulty estimation, holdout validation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_generated\": 500,\n      \"n_items_passing_face_validity\": 312,\n      \"face_validity_pass_rate\": 0.624,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_prompt_based\": 0.31,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_student_sim\": 0.52,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_target\": 0.75,\n      \"subject_coverage_pct\": 89,\n      \"cognitive_level_match_pct\": 67,\n      \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.48,\n      \"discrimination_match_r\": 0.29,\n      \"construct_drift_detected_pct\": 18.4,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 178\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Item Generation Quality Metrics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"Target\",\n          \"Status\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Face validity pass rate\",\n            0.624,\n            \">0.80\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Difficulty ρ (prompt-based)\",\n            0.31,\n            \"0.45+\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Difficulty ρ (student sim)\",\n            0.52,\n            \"0.75+\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Discrimination match r\",\n            0.29,\n            \">0.60\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Construct drift\",\n            \"18.4%\",\n            \"<5%\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Holdout ranking ρ\",\n            0.48,\n            \"≥0.95\",\n            \"FAIL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Item generation失败在worst tier reframe中不造成额外伤害——regeneration（Claim 3 原版）已经在Dream #3中被pruned to appendix。但这个negative result本身有publication value作为\\\"cautionary tale about LLM-based item generation for high-stakes benchmarks\\\"——如果space permits可以在Discussion中brief mention。\\n\\n\\nItem generation面临两个层面的困难。First, face validity：只有62.4%的generated items通过human evaluation（incorrect distractors太obvious，或者stem在语义上 偏移了原item的construct）。Second, calibration：student simulation的difficulty estimation（ρ=0.52）远低于arXiv 2601.09953报告的0.75-0.82，这是因为MMLU items 的difficulty主要由knowledge specificity驱动（而非reasoning complexity），而LLM student simulation更擅长估计reasoning difficulty。Discrimination match更差 （r=0.29）——generated items的区分度系统性偏低，因为LLM倾向于生成\\\"textbook-style\\\" 的clean items而非real exam的nuanced items。\\n18.4%的construct drift意味着近五分之一的生成items实际上测量的是不同的construct—— 比如原item测试\\\"specific legal precedent knowledge\\\"但generated item测试 \\\"general legal reasoning\\\"。这在holdout panel上表现为ρ=0.48——生成的benchmark 与原始benchmark的model ranking correlation很弱。\\nCombined with plan_005的equating failure，整个regeneration pipeline（Claim 3原版） 在worst tier下是完全不可行的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006)。4轮successive administrations模拟。Power improvement from evidence accumulation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"individual_admin_power_delta10\": 0.41,\n      \"cumulative_2admin_power_delta10\": 0.52,\n      \"cumulative_3admin_power_delta10\": 0.58,\n      \"cumulative_4admin_power_delta10\": 0.63,\n      \"target_cumulative_3admin_power\": 0.7,\n      \"target_met\": false,\n      \"prior_calibration_error_mean\": 0.23,\n      \"prior_calibration_error_max\": 0.67,\n      \"fpr_inflation_cumulative_4admin\": 0.074,\n      \"bayesian_mh_correlation_flags\": 0.81,\n      \"bayes_factor_median\": 3.2,\n      \"bayes_factor_gt10_pct\": 18.4,\n      \"simulation_n_per_admin\": 200,\n      \"n_items_simulated\": 1000,\n      \"n_administrations\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cumulative Power by Administration\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"N_admins\",\n          \"Power_δ=0.8\",\n          \"Power_δ=1.0\",\n          \"Power_δ=1.4\",\n          \"FPR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.22,\n            0.41,\n            0.68,\n            0.042\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.31,\n            0.52,\n            0.76,\n            0.051\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.37,\n            0.58,\n            0.81,\n            0.063\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.42,\n            0.63,\n            0.84,\n            0.074\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Prior Calibration Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Admin_pair\",\n          \"Prior_mean_error\",\n          \"Prior_var_error\",\n          \"BF_median\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1→2\",\n            0.14,\n            0.08,\n            4.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2→3\",\n            0.21,\n            0.13,\n            3.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3→4\",\n            0.34,\n            0.19,\n            2.7\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bayesian cumulative DIF在worst tier下确认了paper_framing.md的decision to move it to appendix。Power improvement不足以justify complexity increase。 Prior miscalibration问题是fundamental——LLM benchmark \\\"administrations\\\" 不满足Bayesian updating的stationarity assumption。在reframe后，这变成 appendix material：\\\"simulation study showing theoretical potential with caveats about non-stationary populations\\\"。\\n\\n\\nCumulative Bayesian方法的power improvement低于理论预期：3-admin cumulative power=0.58（vs target 0.70），4-admin才达到0.63。差距来自prior miscalibration： Sinharay et al.的priors是为human testing设计的（student populations with stable demographics），LLM \\\"administrations\\\"的cohort composition变化更剧烈 （每轮新模型的ability distribution shift更大），导致informative priors反而 引入bias。Prior calibration error mean=0.23意味着prior对DIF effect size的 预期系统性偏离了actual，累积后bias不是减少而是compound。\\nBayes factors偏弱（median=3.2，只有18.4%的items BF>10），说明evidence accumulation受限于LLM cohort间的non-stationarity。FPR inflation到0.074 在4-admin后是manageable但concerning——累积更多administrations可能会worse。\\n与MH flags的correlation=0.81说明Bayesian方法在很大程度上agree with MH， 增量贡献有限——essentially adding computational complexity for modest gain。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Benchmark validity under progressive item replacement。Ranking stability, score reliability, construct coverage at 5/10/20/50% replacement。 Theoretical bounds + empirical validation on METABENCH。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rho_5pct_replacement\": 0.993,\n      \"rho_10pct_replacement\": 0.984,\n      \"rho_20pct_replacement\": 0.961,\n      \"rho_50pct_replacement\": 0.887,\n      \"reliability_original_kr20\": 0.967,\n      \"reliability_5pct\": 0.964,\n      \"reliability_10pct\": 0.958,\n      \"reliability_20pct\": 0.943,\n      \"reliability_50pct\": 0.891,\n      \"construct_coverage_original\": 1.0,\n      \"construct_coverage_5pct\": 0.98,\n      \"construct_coverage_10pct\": 0.95,\n      \"construct_coverage_20pct\": 0.87,\n      \"construct_coverage_50pct\": 0.71,\n      \"theoretical_lower_bound_rho_at_31pct\": 0.92,\n      \"empirical_rho_at_31pct\": 0.94,\n      \"critical_replacement_threshold\": 0.23,\n      \"validity_degradation_rate\": \"nonlinear\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Validity Metrics Under Progressive Replacement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Replace_pct\",\n          \"Rank_ρ\",\n          \"KR-20\",\n          \"Coverage\",\n          \"Max_rank_shift\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0% (original)\",\n            1.0,\n            0.967,\n            1.0,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            0.993,\n            0.964,\n            0.98,\n            23\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.984,\n            0.958,\n            0.95,\n            47\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.961,\n            0.943,\n            0.87,\n            112\n          ],\n          [\n            \"31% (DIF rate)\",\n            0.94,\n            0.927,\n            0.79,\n            189\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            0.887,\n            0.891,\n            0.71,\n            341\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Theoretical vs Empirical Degradation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Replace_pct\",\n          \"Theory_lower_ρ\",\n          \"Empirical_ρ\",\n          \"Gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.978,\n            0.984,\n            \"+0.006\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.944,\n            0.961,\n            \"+0.017\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"31%\",\n            0.92,\n            0.94,\n            \"+0.020\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            0.868,\n            0.887,\n            \"+0.019\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation在worst tier reframe中降级为supplementary analysis。 核心insight（replacement threshold < DIF rate）在appendix中作为\\\"the fundamental tension in DIF-based benchmark maintenance\\\"讨论，但不作为main claim。ρ≈0.997 的existing finding（plan_017, DIF removal without replacement）remains the stronger and simpler message for the main paper。\\n\\n\\nGraceful degradation分析本身产生reasonable results——rankings在20%替换时 仍robust（ρ=0.961），但construct coverage更fragile（0.87 at 20%）。关键 问题在worst tier context中：这个分析假设replacement items是well-calibrated的， 但plan_005（equating failure）和plan_006（generation failure）已经证明 实际的replacement items质量远低于预期。所以degradation curves是optimistic lower bound——实际degradation会worse。\\nCritical replacement threshold=23%意味着替换>23%的items时validity开始 non-linearly degrade。但我们的DIF flag rate是31%——超过了这个threshold。 Reviewer会指出：\\\"你说31%的items unstable，但你也说替换>23%就会degrade validity——那你的解决方案（替换flagged items）本身就会destroy benchmark validity。 这不是一个solution而是一个dilemma。\\\"\\n在worst tier reframe中这个dilemma变成feature而非bug：\\\"we characterize the replacement feasibility boundary\\\"——但reviewer可能视其为研究without actionable outcome。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger 2016) as alternative to categorical cohort DIF。 Release date as continuous covariate。Detection power comparison vs categorical DIF。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ift_items_flagged_pct\": 27.4,\n      \"ift_mh_overlap_jaccard\": 0.63,\n      \"ift_unique_flags_pct\": 8.1,\n      \"mh_unique_flags_pct\": 11.7,\n      \"ift_detection_power_delta14\": 0.59,\n      \"mh_detection_power_delta14\": 0.68,\n      \"ift_fpr\": 0.088,\n      \"mh_fpr_temporal\": 0.314,\n      \"ift_tree_depth_median\": 3,\n      \"ift_tree_depth_max\": 7,\n      \"ift_primary_split_variable\": \"release_date\",\n      \"ift_secondary_split\": \"model_size\",\n      \"overfitting_cv_auroc_gap\": 0.12,\n      \"n_stable_splits\": 4,\n      \"n_unstable_splits\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"IFT\",\n          \"MH (temporal)\",\n          \"Advantage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Items flagged %\",\n            27.4,\n            31.3,\n            \"IFT (fewer)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.088,\n            0.314,\n            \"IFT ×3.6 better\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TPR (δ≥1.4)\",\n            0.59,\n            0.68,\n            \"MH +0.09\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Overlap (Jaccard)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.63\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CV stability\",\n            0.67,\n            \"N/A (parametric)\",\n            \"MH\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"IFT Split Stability (Bootstrap)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Split_depth\",\n          \"Variable\",\n          \"Bootstrap_reproduce_pct\",\n          \"Stable\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            \"release_date\",\n            98,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"model_size\",\n            72,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            \"training_data_size\",\n            61,\n            \"Borderline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"subject_category\",\n            34,\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"IFT在worst tier reframe中有niche价值：它提供release_date作为continuous covariate的evidence，支持\\\"temporal instability is real\\\"的narrative。但 overfitting和power loss使其不适合作为primary method。Appendix material。\\n\\n\\nItem-Focused Trees在worst tier下产生mixed results。优点：FPR=0.088远低于 MH temporal的0.314，因为trees不需要硬性cohort split——continuous release date 允许更nuanced的grouping。缺点：detection power=0.59低于MH的0.68，因为trees 将sample分割成更小的subgroups（每个leaf node N更小）。Jaccard=0.63的overlap 说明两种方法largely agree但有meaningful disagreement。\\n关键weakness：overfitting。CV AUROC gap=0.12说明trees在training上over-optimize。 12个split中8个是unstable的（bootstrap resample后不reproduce）。这使得IFT results在robustness上不如MH（MH虽然crude但statistically principled）。\\nReviewer在worst tier下会指出：\\\"IFT有更好的FPR但更差的power和更差的stability—— 这不是一个improvement而是一个tradeoff，你没有demonstrate哪个tradeoff更 appropriate for this application。\\\"\\nPrimary split on release_date confirms temporal effect is real but secondary split on model_size introduces a confound MH doesn't have——larger models are more recent AND better, so tree conflates time and capability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Architecture-homogeneous DIF。Decoder-only subset。IRT fit diagnostics。 Compare FPR/TPR vs full-population DIF。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_decoder_only\": 5226,\n      \"n_non_decoder\": 1,\n      \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n      \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"full_population_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n      \"removed_model\": \"RWKV-v5-Eagle-7B\",\n      \"rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.089,\n      \"rmsea_full\": 0.089,\n      \"cfi_decoder_only\": 0.41,\n      \"cfi_full\": 0.41,\n      \"lz_pct_misfit_decoder_only\": 97.8,\n      \"lz_pct_misfit_full\": 98.1,\n      \"irt_fit_improvement\": \"negligible\",\n      \"temporal_fpr_decoder_only\": 0.313,\n      \"temporal_tpr_p05_decoder_only\": 0.834\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Architecture Stratification Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Full_pop (N=5227)\",\n          \"Decoder-only (N=5226)\",\n          \"Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ETS C%\",\n            31.3,\n            31.3,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Jaccard vs full\",\n            \"—\",\n            1.0,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RMSEA\",\n            0.089,\n            0.089,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CFI\",\n            0.41,\n            0.41,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"|Lz|>2 %\",\n            98.1,\n            97.8,\n            -0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR (temporal)\",\n            0.314,\n            0.313,\n            -0.001\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Non-decoder Model Impact\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Effect_on_C%\",\n          \"Effect_on_rankings\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RWKV-v5-Eagle-7B\",\n            \"RWKV (linear attention)\",\n            \"None\",\n            \"None\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Architecture stratification是一个\\\"dissolved concern\\\"——architecture不是问题， 但IRT misfit仍然是。在worst tier reframe中：(1)architecture section变成一段话 而非一节——\\\"concern dissolved, 99.98% decoder-only\\\"；(2)IRT misfit discussion 变得更prominent——\\\"we acknowledge 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU; total-score conditioning is our pragmatic choice; multidimensional IRT is future work\\\"；(3)这个limitation是honest but costly——reviewer can use it to question the entire DIF analysis。Practitioner's Guide section mitigates by providing \\\"when/how to use DIF despite IRT limitations\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMETABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only（5226/5227），移除1个non-decoder模型 对所有结果的影响为zero（Jaccard=1.000）。Architecture heterogeneity concern dissolved——但这是一个trivial result，不是一个victory。\\n关键问题：IRT fit完全没有improve（RMSEA=0.089, CFI=0.41, 97.8% |Lz|>2）。 这confirms MMLU的IRT misfit不是由architecture heterogeneity造成的——root cause 是multidimensionality（57 subjects）。在worst tier下reviewer的攻击点是： \\\"你证明了architecture不是问题，但IRT misfit仍然devastating。98%的模型misfit 意味着你的ability estimates是meaningless的——MH conditioning on total score 是唯一defensible approach，但total score在multidimensional test上不是ability 的good proxy。So your 31% DIF reflects score-distribution artifacts, not genuine differential item functioning。\\\"\\n这是worst tier核心假设#4的manifestation。Defense只能是承认limitation并argue MH is still the best available tool（\\\"conditioning on total score is imperfect but standard psychometric practice for multidimensional tests\\\"），而非claim results are unaffected。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Semi-synthetic contamination injection into real METABENCH response matrix。 500 clean items, 100-200 injected. TPR/FPR under controlled ground truth。 Vary prevalence (5-30%), exploitation rate (0.4-1.0), focal group size (40-200)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation\": 0.186,\n      \"reviewer_dismissal_probability\": 0.67,\n      \"injection_mechanism_realism_score\": 2.3,\n      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n      \"n_injected_items\": 150,\n      \"exploitation_rate_range\": [\n        0.3,\n        1.0\n      ],\n      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n      \"prevalence_5pct_tpr\": 0.41,\n      \"prevalence_10pct_tpr\": 0.57,\n      \"prevalence_20pct_tpr\": 0.73,\n      \"prevalence_30pct_tpr\": 0.83\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Semi-synthetic Detection Power (Cross-subject Matching)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Exploitation_rate\",\n          \"TPR\",\n          \"ΔTPR\",\n          \"FPR\",\n          \"ΔFPR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"p=0.0 (baseline)\",\n            0.326,\n            0.0,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p=0.3\",\n            0.548,\n            0.222,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p=0.5\",\n            0.834,\n            0.508,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p=0.7\",\n            0.99,\n            0.664,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p=1.0\",\n            1.0,\n            0.674,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Mechanism Realism Critique\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Aspect\",\n          \"Semi-synthetic\",\n          \"Real_contamination\",\n          \"Mismatch\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Signal type\",\n            \"Binary flip\",\n            \"Parametric recall\",\n            \"HIGH\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Response pattern\",\n            \"Only accuracy\",\n            \"Distractor bias\",\n            \"HIGH\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Item correlation\",\n            \"Random selection\",\n            \"Semantic clusters\",\n            \"MEDIUM\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Effect gradient\",\n            \"p ∈ {0,1}\",\n            \"Continuous partial\",\n            \"MEDIUM\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Ability distribution\",\n            \"Real (preserved)\",\n            \"Real\",\n            \"NONE\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic validation在worst tier reframe中的定位shift from \\\"validation of DIF as contamination detector\\\" to \\\"reusable validation infrastructure that any item-level detector can plug into\\\"。ΔTPR methodology和cross-subject matching 是framework contributions that survive mechanism critique。关键修改：(1)不再 claim \\\"DIF can detect real contamination\\\"——而是\\\"DIF can detect differential item functioning under synthetic contamination, consistent with but not proof of real-world detection\\\"；(2)explicitly acknowledge injection mechanism limitations in Method section而非buried in limitations；(3)frame cross-subject matching as primary contribution of this experiment——ΔFPR=0.000 across all conditions 是genuinely novel practical insight。\\n\\nDetection metrics本身look strong——ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, clear dose-response, cross-subject matching eliminates FPR inflation（ΔFPR=0.000）。但worst tier 的核心攻击不是metrics而是mechanism validity。\\nReviewer dismissal probability=0.67基于核心假设#6：\\\"flipping incorrect→correct doesn't model real contamination mechanisms\\\"。具体攻击：(1)真实contamination 是memorization——模型在training中多次见到item，导致parameterized recall，表现为 high confidence on specific items而非simple correctness flip；(2)真实contamination 影响response pattern而非just accuracy——contaminated model可能在某些distractors 上有异常pattern（always选A），simple flip不capture这个；(3)partial contamination is not random——contaminated model更可能在semantically similar items上都contaminated （cluster structure），而random sampling的injection忽略了这个structure； (4)exploitation rate concept假设contamination是binary（correct with probability p）， 但实际是gradient（模型\\\"部分记住\\\"一个item可能表现为distractor bias而非correctness）。\\n\\\"Injection realism score\\\"=2.3/5（hypothetical expert rating）——method是 sound as a statistical framework但ecological validity低。这是worst tier下 ΔTPR被解读为\\\"your framework can detect your artificial signal, but does it detect real contamination?\\\"的核心矛盾。\\nCross-subject matching的ΔFPR=0.000是genuinely novel and survives所有attacks—— 即使injection mechanism被dismissed，matching methodology contribution stands。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1321,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1321}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LM1zXAiVSz6xxP8NV1NwNY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me now write the LaTeX paper. This is a \"worst\" tier paper, which means I need to incorporate the worst-case interpretations of the data while following the narrative guidance.\n\nThe narrative guidance says:\n1. Lead with semi-synthetic validation framework (Claim 3) as primary methodological contribution\n2. Reposition Claim 1 as case study motivating the framework\n3. Drop GSM1K correlation entirely from main paper\n4. Report MH AND SIBTEST jointly; present instability as \"≥18-31% depending on DIF type and threshold\"\n\n\n5. Strengthen the circularity ablation and redundancy finding with that near-perfect correlation\n6. Keep the ground truth meta-critique as a core argument\n7. Add \"Practitioner's Guide\" section\n8. Target ICLR 2027\n\nI need to structure the paper to cover all the experiments: the real data DIF analysis with both MH and SIBTEST, the RL robustness validation results (which go to limitations or appendix per guidance), the ConStat and DVD comparisons, ensemble fusion results (appendix), and the remaining cross-validation experiments.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the full experimental coverage—GSM8K replication without the GSM1K correlation piece, the bifactor IRT equating pilot for limitations, item generation calibration work, Bayesian DIF analysis for the appendix, degradation analysis, item-focused trees comparison, architecture stratification, and semi-synthetic contamination validation. The paper structure should flow from abstract through introduction with the \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing, related work, methods covering MH-DIF, SIBTEST, semi-synthetic framework and cross-subject matching, then the experiments section organized to highlight the key findings while routing supporting 